helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090407.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154347				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090407.xhp\" name=\"Rem Statement [Runtime]\"\>Rem Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090407.xhp	0	help	par_id3153525				0	ca-XR	Specifies that a program line is a comment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090407.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090407.xhp	0	help	par_id3154141				0	ca-XR	Rem Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090407.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151042				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090407.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any text that serves as a comment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090407.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318				0	ca-XR	You can use the single quotation mark instead of the Rem keyword to indicate that the text on a line is comments. This symbol can be inserted directly to the right of the program code, followed by a comment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090407.xhp	0	help	par_id6187017				0	ca-XR	You can use a space followed by the underline character _ as the last two characters of a line to continue the logical line on the next line. To continue comment lines, you must enter "Option Compatible" in the same Basic module.				20200411 15:09:53
