helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	ca-XR	Method of the com.sun.star.container.XContainerListener interface				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	ca-XR	elementReplaced:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	ca-XR	Method of the com.sun.star.container.XContainerListener interface				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	ca-XR	In this example, the prefix is ContListener_. The following subroutines must therefore be implemented in Basic:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	ca-XR	ContListener_disposing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146923				0	ca-XR	ContListener_elementInserted				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318				0	ca-XR	ContListener_elementRemoved				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	ca-XR	ContListener_elementReplaced				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	ca-XR	An event structure type that contains information about an event exists for every Listener type. When a Listener method is called, an instance of this event is passed to the method as a parameter. Basic Listener methods can also call these event objects, so long as the appropriate parameter is passed in the Sub declaration. For example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	ca-XR	Sub ContListener_disposing( oEvent )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	ca-XR	MsgBox "disposing"				20200411 15:09:53
