helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148932				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010201.xhp\" name=\"InputBox Function [Runtime]\"\>InputBox Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151262				0	ca-XR	Displays a prompt in a dialog at which the user can input text. The input is assigned to a variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151100				0	ca-XR	The \<emph\>InputBox\</emph\> statement is a convenient method of entering text through a dialog. Confirm the input by clicking OK or pressing Return. The input is returned as the function return value. If you close the dialog with Cancel, \<emph\>InputBox\</emph\> returns a zero-length string ("").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152347				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201	5			0	ca-XR	InputBox (Msg As String[, Title As String[, Default As String[, x_pos As Integer, y_pos As Integer]]]]) 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150713				0	ca-XR	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
