helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that defines the angle in radians that you want to calculate the sine for.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155413				0	ca-XR	To convert degrees to radians, multiply degrees by Pi/180, and to convert radians to degrees, multiply radians by 180/Pi.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ca-XR	grad=(radiant*180)/pi				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	ca-XR	radiant=(grad*pi)/180				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	ca-XR	Pi is approximately 3.141593.				20200411 15:09:53
