helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	FileAttr-Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153380				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>FileAttr function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153380				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020405.xhp\" name=\"FileAttr-Function [Runtime]\"\>FileAttr Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ca-XR	Returns the access mode or the file access number of a file that was opened with the Open statement. The file access number is dependent on the operating system (OSH = Operating System Handle).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	ca-XR	If you use a 32-Bit operating system, you cannot use the FileAttr-Function to determine the file access number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3163713				0	ca-XR	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020103.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151116				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	ca-XR	FileAttr (FileNumber As Integer, Attribute As Integer)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147349				0	ca-XR	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ca-XR	Integer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153728				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3151074				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> The number of the file that was opened with the Open statement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3144766				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Attribute:\</emph\> Integer expression that indicates the type of file information that you want to return. The following values are possible:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	ca-XR	1: The FileAttr-Function indicates the access mode of the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	ca-XR	2: The FileAttr-Function returns the file access number of the operating system.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	ca-XR	If you specify a parameter attribute with a value of 1, the following return values apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3149124				0	ca-XR	1 - INPUT (file open for input)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	ca-XR	2 - OUTPUT (file open for output)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066				0	ca-XR	4 - RANDOM (file open for random access)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3148406				0	ca-XR	8 - APPEND (file open for appending)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020405.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	ca-XR	32 - BINARY (file open in binary mode).				20200411 15:09:53
