helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869	9			0	ca-XR	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>TimeSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the minute of the serial time value that is generated by the \<emph\>TimeSerial\</emph\> or the \<emph\>TimeValue \</emph\>function. For example, the expression:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	ca-XR	Print Minute(TimeSerial(12,30,41))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	ca-XR	returns the value 30.				20200411 15:09:53
