helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	ca-XR	The natural logarithm is the logarithm to the base e. Base e is a constant with an approximate value of 2.718282...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	ca-XR	You can calculate logarithms to any base (n) for any number (x) by dividing the natural logarithm of x by the natural logarithm of n, as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
