helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>If statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154422				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090101.xhp\" name=\"If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\"\>If...Then...Else Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	ca-XR	Defines one or more statement blocks that you only want to execute if a given condition is True.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	ca-XR	If condition=true Then Statement block [ElseIf condition=true Then] Statement block [Else] Statement block EndIf\<br/\>Instead of Else If you can write ElseIf, instead of End If you can write EndIf.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	ca-XR	The \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statement executes program blocks depending on given conditions. When $[officename] Basic encounters an \<emph\>If\</emph\> statement, the condition is tested. If the condition is True, all subsequent statements up to the next \<emph\>Else\</emph\> or \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement are executed. If the condition is False, and an \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statement follows, $[officename] Basic tests the next condition and executes the following statements if the condition is True. If False, the program continues either with the next \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> or \<emph\>Else\</emph\> statement. Statements following \<emph\>Else\</emph\> are executed only if none of the previously tested conditions were True. After all conditions are evaluated, and the corresponding statements executed, the program continues with the statement following \<emph\>EndIf\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ca-XR	You can nest multiple \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> statements.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Else\</emph\> and \<emph\>ElseIf\</emph\> statements are optional.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152939				0	ca-XR	You can use \<emph\>GoTo\</emph\> and \<emph\>GoSub\</emph\> to jump out of an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> block, but not to jump into an \<emph\>If...Then\</emph\> structure.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	ca-XR	The following example enables you to enter the expiration date of a product, and determines if the expiration date has passed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152576				0	ca-XR	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011				0	ca-XR	Sub ExampleIfThenDate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	ca-XR	Dim sDate as String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	ca-XR	Dim sToday as String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	ca-XR	sDate = InputBox("Enter the expiration date (MM.DD.YYYY)")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	ca-XR	sDate = Right$(sDate, 4) + Mid$(sDate, 4, 2) + Left$(sDate, 2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	ca-XR	sToday = Date$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	ca-XR	sToday = Right$(sToday, 4)+ Mid$(sToday, 4, 2) + Left$(sToday, 2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154792				0	ca-XR	If sDate < sToday Then				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155601				0	ca-XR	MsgBox "The expiration date has passed"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	ca-XR	ElseIf sDate > sToday Then				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146912				0	ca-XR	MsgBox "The expiration date has not yet passed"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153710				0	ca-XR	Else				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	ca-XR	MsgBox "The expiration date is today"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	ca-XR	End If				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	ca-XR	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
