helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146117				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03060100.xhp\" name=\"AND Operator [Runtime]\"\>AND Operator [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143268				0	ca-XR	Logically combines two expressions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344				0	ca-XR	Result = Expression1 And Expression2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Result:\</emph\> Any numeric variable that records the result of the combination.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any expressions that you want to combine.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156215				0	ca-XR	Boolean expressions combined with AND only return the value \<emph\>True\</emph\> if both expressions evaluate to \<emph\>True\</emph\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>True\</emph\> AND \<emph\>True\</emph\> returns \<emph\>True\</emph\>; for all other combinations the result is \<emph\>False\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	ca-XR	The AND operator also performs a bitwise comparison of identically positioned bits in two numeric expressions.				20200411 15:09:53
