helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Date Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156027				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>Date statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156027				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030301.xhp\" name=\"Date Statement [Runtime]\"\>Date Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291				0	ca-XR	Returns the current system date as a string, or resets the date. The date format depends on your local system settings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148686				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	ca-XR	Date ; Date = Text As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154347				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Only required in order to reset the system date. In this case, the string expression must correspond to the date format defined in your local settings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793				0	ca-XR	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	ca-XR	Sub ExampleDate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	ca-XR	msgbox "The date is " & Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030301.xhp	0	help	par_id3145174				0	ca-XR	end sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Erase Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104700.xhp	0	help	bm_id624713				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>Erase function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10548				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03104700.xhp\"\>Erase Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10558				0	ca-XR	Erases the contents of array elements of fixed size arrays, and releases the memory used by arrays of variable size.				20200411 15:09:53
