helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104700.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E6				0	ca-XR	Erase Arraylist				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104700.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E9				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03104700.xhp	0	help	par_idN105ED				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Arraylist\</emph\> - The list of arrays to be erased.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Converting Date Values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030100.xhp\" name=\"Converting Date Values\"\>Converting Date Values\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	ca-XR	The following functions convert date values to calculable numbers and back.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	TimeSerial Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143271				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>TimeSerial function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143271				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030205.xhp\" name=\"TimeSerial Function [Runtime]\"\>TimeSerial Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344				0	ca-XR	Calculates a serial time value for the specified hour, minute, and second parameters that are passed as numeric value. You can then use this value to calculate the difference between times.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146794				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	ca-XR	TimeSerial (hour, minute, second)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	ca-XR	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	ca-XR	Date				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153193				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>hour:\</emph\> Any integer expression that indicates the hour of the time that is used to determine the serial time value. Valid values: 0-23.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>minute:\</emph\> Any integer expression that indicates the minute of the time that is used to determine the serial time value. In general, use values between 0 and 59. However, you can also use values that lie outside of this range, where the number of minutes influence the hour value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3161831				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>second:\</emph\> Any integer expression that indicates the second of the time that is used to determine the serial time value. In general, you can use values between 0 and 59. However, you can also use values that lie outside of this range, where the number seconds influences the minute value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Examples:\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153952				0	ca-XR	12, -5, 45 corresponds to 11, 55, 45				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349				0	ca-XR	12, 61, 45 corresponds to 13, 2, 45				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3147426				0	ca-XR	12, 20, -2 corresponds to 12, 19, 58				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153365				0	ca-XR	12, 20, 63 corresponds to 12, 21, 4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	ca-XR	You can use the TimeSerial function to convert any time into a single value that you can use to calculate time differences.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3155308				0	ca-XR	The TimeSerial function returns the type Variant with VarType 7 (Date). This value is stored internally as a double-precision number between 0 and 0.9999999999. As opposed to the DateSerial or DateValue function, where the serial date values are calculated as days relative to a fixed date, you can calculate with values returned by the TimeSerial function, but you cannot evaluate them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3149482				0	ca-XR	In the TimeValue function, you can pass a string as a parameter containing the time. For the TimeSerial function, however, you can pass the individual parameters (hour, minute, second) as separate numeric expressions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154790				0	ca-XR	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ca-XR	Sub ExampleTimeSerial				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	ca-XR	Dim dDate As Double, sDate As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	ca-XR	dDate = TimeSerial(8,30,15)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	ca-XR	sDate = TimeSerial(8,30,15)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	ca-XR	MsgBox dDate,64,"Time as a number"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	ca-XR	MsgBox sDate,64,"Formatted time"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030205.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836				0	ca-XR	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	CDateFromIso Function [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153127				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>CdateFromIso function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030108.xhp\" name=\"CDateFromIso Function [Runtime]\"\>CDateFromIso Function [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	ca-XR	Returns the internal date number from a string that contains a date in ISO format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148947				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	ca-XR	CDateFromIso(String)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154367				0	ca-XR	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	ca-XR	Internal date number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125864				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>String:\</emph\> A string that contains a date in ISO format. The year may have two or four digits.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	ca-XR	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318				0	ca-XR	dateval = CDateFromIso("20021231")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030108.xhp	0	help	par_id3146921				0	ca-XR	returns 12/31/2002 in the date format of your system				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	IIf Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155420				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>IIf statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155420				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03090103.xhp\" name=\"IIf Statement [Runtime]\"\>IIf Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	ca-XR	Returns one of two possible function results, depending on the logical value of the evaluated expression.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159413				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	ca-XR	IIf (Expression, ExpressionTrue, ExpressionFalse)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150541				0	ca-XR	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Expression:\</emph\> Any expression that you want to evaluate. If the expression evaluates to \<emph\>True\</emph\>, the function returns the result of ExpressionTrue, otherwise it returns the result of ExpressionFalse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>ExpressionTrue, ExpressionFalse:\</emph\> Any expression, one of which will be returned as the function result, depending on the logical evaluation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	MsgBox Statement [Runtime]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	bm_id1807916				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>MsgBox statement\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010101.xhp\"\>MsgBox Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148947				0	ca-XR	Displays a dialog box containing a message.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153897				0	ca-XR	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	ca-XR	MsgBox Text As String [,Type As Integer [,Dialogtitle As String]] (As Statement) or MsgBox (Text As String [,Type As Integer [,Dialogtitle As String]]) (As Function)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	ca-XR	Parameter:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798	6			0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Text\</emph\>: String expression displayed as a message in the dialog box. Line breaks can be inserted with Chr$(13).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150769	7			0	ca-XR	\<emph\>DialogTitle\</emph\>: String expression displayed in the title bar of the dialog. If omitted, the title bar displays the name of the respective application.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228	8			0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Type\</emph\>: Any integer expression that specifies the dialog type, as well as the number and type of buttons to display, and the icon type. \<emph\>Type\</emph\> represents a combination of bit patterns, that is, a combination of elements can be defined by adding their respective values:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3161832				0	ca-XR	0 : Display OK button only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ca-XR	1 : Display OK and Cancel buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149665				0	ca-XR	2 : Display Abort, Retry, and Ignore buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318				0	ca-XR	3 : Display Yes, No and Cancel buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155412				0	ca-XR	4 : Display Yes and No buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	ca-XR	5 : Display Retry and Cancel buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	ca-XR	16 : Add the Stop icon to the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	ca-XR	32 : Add the Question icon to the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
