helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090301.xhp	0	help	par_id3147318				0	ca-XR	The \<emph\>GoSub\</emph\> statement calls a local subroutine indicated by a label from within a subroutine or a function. The name of the label must end with a colon (":").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03090301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	ca-XR	If the program encounters a Return statement not preceded by \<emph\>GoSub\</emph\>, $[officename] Basic returns an error message. Use \<emph\>Exit Sub\</emph\> or \<emph\>Exit Function\</emph\> to ensure that the program leaves a Sub or Function before reaching the next Return statement.				20200411 15:09:53
