helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055A				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/symbolshapes.xhp\"\>Symbol Shapes\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056A				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Symbol Shapes toolbar from which you can insert graphics into your document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EB				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an icon on the Symbol Shapes toolbar, and then drag in the document to draw the shape.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\symbolshapes.xhp	0	help	par_idN1059D				0	ca-XR	Some shapes have a special handle which you can drag to change the properties of the shape. The mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol over these special handles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	General				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152551				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>submitting forms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>get method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>post method for form transmissions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>General\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	ca-XR	A form is a text document or spreadsheet with different form controls. If you create a form for a Web page, the user can enter data into it to send over the Internet. The data from the form controls of a form is transmitted to a server by specifying a URL and can be processed on the server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149283				0	ca-XR	Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150789				0	ca-XR	Specifies a name for the form. This name is used to identify the form in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170600.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigator\"\>Form Navigator\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152425				0	ca-XR	URL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	ca-XR	Specifies the URL to which the data of the completed form is to be transmitted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154751				0	ca-XR	Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	ca-XR	Defines the target frame in which the loaded URL is to appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152551				0	ca-XR	Type of submission				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_METHOD\"\>Specifies the method to transfer the completed form information.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145065				0	ca-XR	Using the "Get" method, the data of every control is transmitted as an environment variable. They are appended to the URL in the form "?Control1=Content1&Control2=Content2&..."; the character string is analyzed by a program on the recipient's server.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	ca-XR	Using the "Post" method, a document is created from the content of the form that is sent to the specified URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	ca-XR	Submission encoding				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SUBMIT_ENCODING\"\>Specifies the type for encoding the data transfer.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155419				0	ca-XR	Data transfer of control information				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153717				0	ca-XR	When sending a form, all controls available in $[officename] are taken into consideration. The name of the control and the corresponding value, if available, are transmitted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	ca-XR	Which values are transmitted in each case depends on the respective control. For text fields, the visible entries are transmitted; for list boxes, the selected entries are transmitted; for check boxes and option fields, the associated reference values are transmitted if these fields were activated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	ca-XR	How this information is transmitted depends on the selected transfer method (Get or Post) and the coding (URL or Multipart). If the Get method and URL encoding are selected, for example, value pairs in the form <Name>=<Value> are sent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3157909				0	ca-XR	In addition to the controls that are recognized in HTML, $[officename] offers other controls. It should be noted that, for fields with a specific numerical format, the visible values are not transmitted but rather fixed default formats. The following table shows how the data of the $[officename]-specific controls is transmitted:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153698				0	ca-XR	Control				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	ca-XR	Value Pair				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153823				0	ca-XR	Numeric field, currency field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734				0	ca-XR	A decimal separator is always displayed as a period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563				0	ca-XR	Date field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3146794				0	ca-XR	The date format is sent in a fixed format (MM-DD-YYYY), regardless of the user's local settings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	ca-XR	Time field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779				0	ca-XR	The time format is sent in a fixed format (HH:MM:SS), regardless of the user's local settings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361				0	ca-XR	Pattern field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	ca-XR	The values of pattern fields are sent as text fields, that is, the value visible in the form is sent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	ca-XR	Table control				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ca-XR	From the table control, the individual columns are always transmitted. The name of the control, the name of the column, and the value of the column are sent. Using the Get method with URL encoding, the transmission is done in the form <Name of the table control>.<Name of the column>=<Value>, for example, with the value being dependent on the column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Add Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170400.xhp\" name=\"Add Field\"\>Add Field\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"text\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AddField\"\>Opens a window where you can select a database field to add to the form or report.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FIELD_SEL\"\>The field selection window lists all database fields of the table or query that was specified as the data source in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3147620				0	ca-XR	You can insert a field into the current document by dragging and dropping. A field is then inserted which contains a link to the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170400.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	ca-XR	If you add fields to a form and you switch off the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"Design Mode\"\>Design Mode\</link\>, you can see that $[officename] adds a labeled input field for every inserted database field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Combo Box/List Box Wizard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159233				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>forms; Combo Box/List Box Wizard\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154094				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box/List Box Wizard\"\>Combo Box/List Box Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	ca-XR	If you insert a combo box or a list box in a document, a wizard starts automatically. This wizard allows you to interactively specify which information is shown.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145211				0	ca-XR	You can use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171100.xhp\" name=\"Wizards On/Off\"\>\<emph\>Wizards On/Off\</emph\>\</link\> icon to keep the wizard from starting automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391				0	ca-XR	The wizards for combo boxes and list boxes differ from each other in their final step. This is because the nature of control fields:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>List Boxes\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	ca-XR	In the case of a list box, the user selects one entry from a list of entries. These entries are saved in a database table and cannot be modified through the list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	ca-XR	As a general rule, the database table that contains the visible list entries in the form is not the table on which the form is based. The list boxes in a form work by using references; that is, references to the visible list entries are located in the form table (values table) and are also entered as such in the values table if the user selects an entry from the list and saves it. Through reference values, list boxes can display data from a table linked to the current form table. Thus the \<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\> allows two tables of a database to be linked, so that the control field can display a detailed list of a database field that is located in a different table from the one to which the form refers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	ca-XR	In the other tables the required field is searched for by using the field names (ControlSource) and then the fields will be completed accordingly. If the field name is not found, the list will remain empty. When list fields contain linked columns, the first column of the other table will be used without a query being shown first.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	ca-XR	If an article table contains, for example, the number of a supplier, the list box can use the "Supplier number" link to display the name of the supplier from the supplier table. On the \<emph\>Field links\</emph\> page the Wizard will ask you about all the settings required for this link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150977				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Combo Boxes\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	ca-XR	In the case of combo boxes, users can select one entry from the list entries or enter text themselves. The entries, which are offered as a list from which users can select, may originate from any database table. The entries that users select or enter so that they can be saved can be saved either in the form only, or in a database. If they are saved in a database, they will be written to the database table on which the form is based.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	ca-XR	Combo boxes can display the data of any table. A direct link between the current form table and the table whose values are to be displayed in the combo box (list table) is not required. Combo boxes do not work with references. If the user enters or selects a value and saves it, the value actually displayed will be entered in the form table. As there is no link between the form table and the list table, the \<emph\>Field Link\</emph\> table does not appear here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170900.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	ca-XR	In the case of a list box, you select entries from the list, and these are saved in the list table. In the case of a combo box, you can add additional text that can be written to the current database table of the form (values table) and stored there as desired. For this function, the \<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\> has the \<emph\>Data Processing\</emph\> page as the last page, whereas in the case of list boxes this page does not exist. Here you can enter whether and where text that has been entered is to be saved in the values table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Add Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>tables in databases; adding to queries\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788				0	ca-XR	Add Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152821	2			0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"tabellehinzufuegentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_JOINSH_ADDTAB_TABLELIST\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the tables to be inserted into the design window.\</ahelp\> In the\<emph\> Add Tables \</emph\>dialog, select the tables you need for your current task. \</variable\> When creating a query or a new table presentation, select the corresponding table to which the query or table presentation should refer. When working with relational databases, select the tables between which you want to build relationships.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760				0	ca-XR	The inserted tables appear in a separate window in the query design or relational windows, along with a list of the fields contained in the table. You can determine the size and order of this window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927				0	ca-XR	Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091208059				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows only tables.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200912080616				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows only queries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150713				0	ca-XR	Table name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156042				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_JOINSH_ADDTAB_TABLELIST\"\>Lists the available tables.\</ahelp\> To insert a table, select one from the list and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. You can also double-click the table name, and a window will be displayed containing the table fields at the top of the query design or the relational window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151226				0	ca-XR	Add				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153683				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_PUSHBUTTON_DLG_JOIN_TABADD_PB_ADDTABLE\"\>Inserts the currently selected table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153527				0	ca-XR	Close				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_JOINSH_ADDTAB_CLOSE\"\>Closes the \<emph\>Add Tables\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
