helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	2			0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"form\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormProperties\" visibility=\"visible\"\>In this dialog you can specify, among others,  the data source and the events for the whole form.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Font Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148983				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>fonts; specifying several\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>alternative fonts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; alternative fonts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150808				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02020000.xhp\" name=\"Font Name\"\>Font Name\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156414				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"schriftarttext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CharFontName\"\>Allows you to select a font name from the list or enter a font name directly.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	ca-XR	You can enter several fonts, separated by semicolons. $[officename] uses each named font in succession if the previous fonts are not available.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	ca-XR	Any font changes apply to the selected text or word in which the cursor is positioned. If no text has been selected, the font applies to text typed afterwards.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155941				0	ca-XR	The last five font names that have been selected are shown in the top part of the combo box, if you have marked the \<emph\>Font history\</emph\> field in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - View\</emph\>. As soon as you close your document, the normal alphabetic numbering of the installed fonts will be recreated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3154810\" src=\"res/helpimg/swh00055.png\" width=\"2.028in\" height=\"0.292in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154810\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150085				0	ca-XR	Font Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	ca-XR	In $[officename] you see the available fonts only if a printer is installed as the default printer in your system. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>With the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\" name=\"spadmin\"\>spadmin\</link\> program you can define a printer as the default printer. \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>In order to install a printer as the default printer please refer to your operating system documentation.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"vorschautext\"\>You can see the name of the fonts formatted in their respective font if you mark the \<emph\>Preview in fonts lists\</emph\> field in \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - View\"\>$[officename] - View\</link\> in the Options dialog box.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\02020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154125				0	ca-XR	If you receive an error message that states that certain fonts have not been found, you can install them with \<emph\>$[officename] Setup\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Repair\</emph\> mode if it is a $[officename] font.				20200411 15:09:53
