helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146936				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"datensatzsuche\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"Find Record\"\>Find Record\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147588				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"suchentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RecSearch\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Searches database tables and forms.\</ahelp\>In forms or database tables, you can search through data fields, list boxes, and check boxes for specific values. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	ca-XR	When searching a table, the data fields of the current table are searched. When searching in a form, the data fields of the table linked with the form are searched.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	ca-XR	The search described here is carried out by \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>. If you want to use the SQL server to search in a database, then you should use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"Form-based Filters\"\>Form-based Filters\</link\> icon on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	ca-XR	The search function is also available for table controls. When calling the search function from a table control, you can search each column of the table control corresponding to the database columns of the linked database table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	ca-XR	Search for				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	ca-XR	Specifies the type of search.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153683				0	ca-XR	Text:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORTEXT\"\>Enter the search term in the box or select it from the list.\</ahelp\> The text under the cursor is already copied into the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> combo box. Note that while running a search in a form, tabs and line breaks cannot be processed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	ca-XR	Your search terms will be saved as long as the table or the formula document is open. If you are running more than one search and you would like to repeat the search term, you can select a previously used search term from the combo box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	ca-XR	Field content is NULL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153543				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain no data.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153717				0	ca-XR	Field content is not NULL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SEARCHFORNOTNULL\"\>Specifies that fields will be found that contain data.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156153				0	ca-XR	Where to search				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	ca-XR	Specifies the fields for the search.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154564				0	ca-XR	Form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_LB_FORM\"\>Specifies the logical form in which you want the search to take place.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	107			0	ca-XR	The\<emph\> Form \</emph\>combo box is only visible if the current document is a form document with more than one logical form. It does not appear during a search in tables or queries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	ca-XR	Form documents may contain multiple logical forms. These are individual form components, which are each linked to a table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086				0	ca-XR	The \<emph\>Form\</emph\> combo box contains the names of all logical forms for which controls exist.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159414				0	ca-XR	All Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_ALLFIELDS\"\>Searches through all fields.\</ahelp\> If you are running a search in a table, all fields in the table will be searched. If you are running a search in a form, all fields of the logical form (entered under \<emph\>Form\</emph\>) will be searched. If you are running a search in a table control field, all columns that are linked to a valid database table field will be searched.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	ca-XR	Note that the fields of the current logical form do not have to be identical to the fields of the form document. If the form document contains fields that point to multiple data sources (that is, multiple logical forms), the \<emph\>All Fields\</emph\> option will only search for the fields linked to data sources in the form document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150865				0	ca-XR	Single field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SINGLEFIELD\"\>Searches through a specified data field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154365				0	ca-XR	Settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158408				0	ca-XR	Defines settings to control the search.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149809				0	ca-XR	Position				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_POSITION\"\>Specifies the relationship of the search term and the field contents.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ca-XR	anywhere in the field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145744				0	ca-XR	Returns all fields containing the search pattern anywhere in the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	ca-XR	beginning of field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	ca-XR	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the beginning of the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	ca-XR	end of field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ca-XR	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the end of the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	ca-XR	entire field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127				0	ca-XR	Returns all fields containing the search pattern as an exact match to the contents of the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	ca-XR	If the \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> check box is marked, this function is not available.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	ca-XR	Apply field format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_FORMATTER\"\>Specifies that all field formats are considered when searching in the current document.\</ahelp\> Field formats are all visible formats that are created using the following possibilities:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	ca-XR	in table design mode for field properties,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	ca-XR	in data source view on column formatting,				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941				0	ca-XR	in forms on control properties.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156736				0	ca-XR	If the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> box is marked, the data source view of the table or form is searched using the formatting set there. If the box is not marked, the database is searched using the formatting saved in the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280				0	ca-XR	Example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	ca-XR	You have a date field, which is saved in "DD.MM.YY" format in the database (for example, 17.02.65). The format of the entry is changed in the data source view to "DD MMM YYYY" (17 Feb 1965). Following this example, a record containing February 17 is only found when the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> option is on:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150593				0	ca-XR	Apply field format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253				0	ca-XR	Search pattern				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3083279				0	ca-XR	on				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155850				0	ca-XR	"Feb" is returned, but not "2".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148590				0	ca-XR	off				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	ca-XR	"2" is returned, but not "Feb".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321				0	ca-XR	It is recommended that you always search using field formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	ca-XR	The following examples show possible issues when searching without field formatting. These issues depend on the database used and only occur for certain internal default formatting:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	ca-XR	Search results				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273				0	ca-XR	Cause				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836				0	ca-XR	"5" returns "14:00:00" as a time				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156332				0	ca-XR	Time fields are not defined for dBASE databases and must be simulated. To internally display the time "14:00:00", a 5 is necessary.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965				0	ca-XR	"00:00:00" returns all records of a standard date field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146081				0	ca-XR	The database stores a date value internally using a combined date/time field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	ca-XR	"45.79" does not return "45.79" although the \<emph\>entire field\</emph\> option is selected under \<emph\>Position\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518				0	ca-XR	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481				0	ca-XR	In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBASE databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	ca-XR	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153355				0	ca-XR	If you are searching the values of check boxes, and \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> is on, then you will receive a "1" for marked check boxes, a "0" for unmarked check boxes, and an empty string for undefined (tristate) check boxes. If the search has been carried out with \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> set to off, you will see the language-dependent default values "TRUE" or "FALSE".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150995	119			0	ca-XR	If you use \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> when searching in list boxes, you find the text displayed in list boxes. If you do not use \<emph\>Apply field format,\</emph\> you will find the contents corresponding to the standard field format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150387				0	ca-XR	Match case				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_CASE\"\>Specifies that upper and lower case are taken into consideration during the search.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145297				0	ca-XR	Search backwards				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151249				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BACKWARD\"\>Specifies that the search process will run in reverse direction, from the last to the first record.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152484				0	ca-XR	From top / From bottom				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_STARTOVER\"\>Restarts the search. A forward search restarts with the first record. A backwards search restarts with the last record.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163724				0	ca-XR	Wildcard expression				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_WILDCARD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows a search with a * or ? wildcard.\</ahelp\> You can use the following wildcards:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146317				0	ca-XR	Wildcards				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	ca-XR	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158411				0	ca-XR	?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874				0	ca-XR	for exactly one arbitrary character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	ca-XR	"?loppy" returns "Floppy"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	ca-XR	"M?ller" returns, for example, Miller and Moller				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148803				0	ca-XR	*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138				0	ca-XR	for 0 or more arbitrary characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	ca-XR	"*-*" returns "ZIP-Drive" and "CD-ROM"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	ca-XR	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145762				0	ca-XR	If you want to search for the actual characters ? or *, preface them with a backslash: "\\?" or "\\*". However, this is only necessary when \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> is enabled. When the option is not enabled, the wildcard characters are processed like normal characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147130				0	ca-XR	Regular expression				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_REGULAR\"\>Searches with regular expressions.\</ahelp\> The same regular expressions that are supported here are also supported in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Find & Replace dialog\"\>Find & Replace dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718				0	ca-XR	Searching with regular expressions offers more options than searching with wildcard expressions. If you search with regular expressions, the following characters correspond to those used in searches with wildcards:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153705				0	ca-XR	Search with wildcard expression				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	ca-XR	Search with regular expressions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151045				0	ca-XR	?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150384				0	ca-XR	.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153793				0	ca-XR	*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150428				0	ca-XR	.*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150861				0	ca-XR	State				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477				0	ca-XR	The \<emph\>State\</emph\> line shows the records returned by the search. If the search reaches the end (or the beginning) of a table, the search is automatically continued at the other end.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720				0	ca-XR	In very large databases, finding the record in reverse search order can take some time. In this case, the status bar informs you that the records are still being counted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147389				0	ca-XR	Search / Cancel				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Starts or cancels the search.\</ahelp\> If the search is successfully completed, the corresponding field in the table is highlighted. You can continue the search by clicking the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> button again. You can cancel a search process by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145080				0	ca-XR	Close				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156166				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_CLOSE\"\>Closes the dialog. The settings of the last search will be saved until you quit \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151183				0	ca-XR	If several tables or forms are open, you can set different search options for each document. When you close the documents only the search options of the document last closed are saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Design Mode On/Off				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"Design Mode On/Off\"\>Design Mode On/Off\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SwitchControlDesignMode\"\>Toggles the Design mode on or off. This function is used to switch quickly between \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Design\"\>Design\</link\> and User mode. Activate to edit the form controls, deactivate to use the form controls.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3153528				0	ca-XR	Please note the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01171000.xhp\" name=\"Open in Design Mode\"\>\<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\>\</link\> function. If \<emph\>Open in Design Mode\</emph\> is activated, the document is always opened in Design mode, regardless of the state in which it is saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ca-XR	If your form is linked to a database and you turn off the Design mode, the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Bar\"\>Form Bar\</link\> is displayed at the lower margin of the document window. You can edit the link to the database in the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Crop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154044				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24100000.xhp\" name=\"Crop\"\>Crop\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154863				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GrafAttrCrop\"\>Allows to crop the display of an inserted picture. Only the display gets cropped, the inserted picture is not changed.\</ahelp\> A picture must be selected to enable cropping.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id0514200804261097				0	ca-XR	In Impress and Draw no dialog is shown when you click the icon, but you see eight cropping handles. Open the context menu of a selected picture and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Crop Picture\</item\>, if you want to use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030800.xhp\"\>dialog\</link\> for cropping.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id0514200804261043				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Drag any of the eight cropping handles to crop the picture.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id0522200809440491				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id0522200809434429\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_crop.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id0522200809434429\"\>icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	ca-XR	Crop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Form-based Filters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147000				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"formfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/02/12110000.xhp\" name=\"Form-based Filters\"\>Form-based Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"formfiltertext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormFilter\"\>Prompts the database server to filter the visible data by specified criteria.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152918				0	ca-XR	Unlike the normal search, which is activated by the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100200.xhp\" name=\"Find Record\"\>Find Record\</link\> icon on the \<emph\>Form\</emph\> Bar, you can search more quickly by using the form-based filter. Usually a quick database server is charged with the search. Also, you can enter more complex search conditions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3147226\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formfilter.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147226\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149751				0	ca-XR	Form-based Filters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>forms; data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; forms and subforms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; subforms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subforms; description\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>Data\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242	2			0	ca-XR	The\<emph\> Data \</emph\>tab page defines the form properties that refer to the database that is linked to the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	ca-XR	Defines the data source on which the form is based, or specifies whether the data can be edited by the user. Apart from the sort and filter functions, you will also find all the necessary properties to create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154810				0	ca-XR	Data source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATASOURCE\"\>Defines the data source to which the form should refer.\</ahelp\> If you click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button, you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, where you can choose a data source.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948				0	ca-XR	Content				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURSORSOURCE\"\>Determines the content to be used for the form. The content can be an existing table or a query (previously created in the database), or it can be defined by an SQL-statement. Before you enter a content you have to define the exact type in \<emph\>Content type\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149657				0	ca-XR	If you have selected either "Table" or "Query" in \<emph\>Content type\</emph\>, the box lists all the tables and queries set up in the selected database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148755				0	ca-XR	Content type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURSORSOURCETYPE\"\>Defines whether the data source is to be an existing database table or query, or if the form is to be generated based on an SQL statement.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ca-XR	If you choose "Table" or "Query", the form will refer to the table or query that you specify under \<emph\>Content\</emph\>. If you want to create a new query or a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, then you have to choose the "SQL" option. You can then enter the statement for the SQL query or the subform directly in the \<emph\>List content\</emph\> box on the Control properties Data tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158409				0	ca-XR	Analyze SQL command				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ESCAPE_PROCESSING\"\>Specifies whether the SQL statement is to be analyzed by %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\> If set to Yes, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button next to the \<emph\>Content\</emph\> list box. This will open a window where you can graphically create a database query. When you close that window, the SQL statement for the created query will be inserted in the \<emph\>Content\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	ca-XR	Filter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FILTER_CRITERIA\"\>Enter the required conditions for filtering the data in the form. The filter specifications follow SQL rules without using the WHERE clause.\</ahelp\> For example, if you want to display all records with the "Mike" forename, type into the data field: Forename = 'Mike'. You can also combine conditions: Forename = 'Mike' OR Forename = 'Peter'. All records matching either of these two conditions will be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	ca-XR	The filter function is available in user mode through the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12030000.xhp\" name=\"AutoFilter\"\>\<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\>\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090000.xhp\" name=\"Default Filter\"\>\<emph\>Default Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icons on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigation Bar\"\>\<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> Bar\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156005				0	ca-XR	Sort				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SORT_CRITERIA\"\>Specifies the conditions to sort the data in the form. The specification of the sorting conditions follows SQL rules without the use of the ORDER BY clause.\</ahelp\> For example, if you want all records of a database to be sorted in one field in an ascending order and in another field in a descending order, enter Forename ASC, Name DESC (presuming Forename and Name are the names of the data fields).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	ca-XR	The appropriate icons on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigation Bar\"\>\<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> Bar\</link\> can be used in User mode to sort: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12010000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Ascending\"\>\<emph\>Sort Ascending\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Descending\"\>\<emph\>Sort Descending\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100100.xhp\" name=\"Sort\"\>\<emph\>Sort\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148616				0	ca-XR	Add data only				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153139				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATAENTRY\"\>Determines if the form only allows the addition of new data (Yes) or if it allows other properties as well (No).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	ca-XR	If \<emph\>Add data only\</emph\> is set to "Yes", changing or deleting data is not possible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148455				0	ca-XR	Navigation bar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157976				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATION\"\>Specifies whether the navigation functions in the lower form bar can be used.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	ca-XR	The "Parent Form" option is used for subforms. If you choose this option for a subform, you can navigate using the records of the main form if the cursor is placed in the subform. A subform is linked to the parent form by a 1:1 relationship, so navigation is always performed in the parent form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151051				0	ca-XR	Cycle				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CYCLE\"\>Determines how the navigation should be done using the tab key.\</ahelp\> Using the tab key, you can move forward in the form. If you simultaneously press the Shift key, the navigation will follow the opposite direction. If you reach the last (or the first) field and press the tab key again, it can have various effects. Define the key control with the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	ca-XR	Option				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150424				0	ca-XR	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150417				0	ca-XR	Default				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157847				0	ca-XR	This setting automatically defines a cycle which follows an existing database link: If the form contains a database link, the Tab key will, by default, initiate a change to the next or previous record on exit from the last field (see All Records). If there is no database link the next/previous form is shown (see Current Page).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	ca-XR	All records				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152972				0	ca-XR	This option applies to database forms only and is used to navigate through all records. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	ca-XR	Active record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145301				0	ca-XR	This option applies to database forms only, and is used to navigate within the current record. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3146913				0	ca-XR	Current page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330				0	ca-XR	On exit from the last field of a form, the cursor skips to the first field in the next form. This is standard for HTML forms; therefore, this option is especially relevant for HTML forms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155064				0	ca-XR	Allow additions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_ADDITIONS\"\>Determines if data can be added.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156054				0	ca-XR	Allow modifications				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156377				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_EDITS\"\> Determines if the data can be modified.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149019				0	ca-XR	Allow deletions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148995				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_DELETIONS\"\>Determines if the data can be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153714				0	ca-XR	Link master fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MASTERFIELDS\"\>If you create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, enter the data field of the parent form responsible for the synchronization between parent and subform.\</ahelp\> To enter multiple values, press Shift + Enter after each input line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	ca-XR	The subform is based on an \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#sql\" name=\"SQL\"\>SQL\</link\> query; more specifically, on a \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Parameter Query\"\>Parameter Query\</link\>. If a field name is entered in the \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> box, the data contained in that field in the main form is read to a variable that you must enter in \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\>. In an appropriate SQL statement, this variable is compared to the table data that the subform refers to. Alternatively, you can enter the column name in the \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156089				0	ca-XR	Consider the following example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	ca-XR	The database table on which the form is based is, for example, a customer database ("Customer"), where every customer has been given a unique number in a data field named "Cust_ID". A customer's orders are maintained in another database table. You now want to see each customer's orders after entering them into the form. In order to do this you should create a subform. Under \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> enter the data field from the customer database which clearly identifies the customer, that is, Cust_ID. Under \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\> enter the name of a variable which is to accept the data of the field Cust_ID, for example, x.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	ca-XR	The subform should show the appropriate data from the orders table ("Orders") for each customer ID (Customer_ID -> x). This is only possible if each order is uniquely assigned to one customer in the orders table. Alternatively, you can use another field called Customer_ID; however, to make sure that this field is not confused with the same field from the main form, the field is called Customer_Number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153537				0	ca-XR	Now compare the Customer_Number in the "Orders" table with the Customer_ID from the "Customers" table, which can be done, for example, using the x variable with the following SQL statement:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	ca-XR	SELECT * FROM Orders WHERE Customer_Number =: x (if you want the subform to show all data from the orders table)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3163727				0	ca-XR	or:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921				0	ca-XR	SELECT Item FROM Orders WHERE Customer_Number =: x (if you want the subform from the orders table to show only the data contained in the "Item" field)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	ca-XR	The SQL statement can either be entered in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> field, or you can create an appropriate parameter query, which can be used to create the subform.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150648				0	ca-XR	Link slave fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149923				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SLAVEFIELDS\"\>If you create a subform, enter the variable where possible values from the parent form field can be stored.\</ahelp\> If a subform is based on a query, enter the variable that you defined in the query. If you create a form using an SQL statement entered in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> field, enter the variable you used in the statement. You can choose any variable name. If you want to enter multiple values, press Shift + Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	ca-XR	If, for example, you specified the Customer_ID database field as a parent field under \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\>, then you can define under \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\> the name of the variable in which the values of the Customer_ID database field are to be stored. If you now specify an SQL statement in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> box using this variable, the relevant values are displayed in the subform.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152778				0	ca-XR	What is a subform?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155579				0	ca-XR	Forms are created based on a database table or database query. They display the data in a visually pleasant fashion and can be used to enter data or edit data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147094	34			0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"wozu\"\>If you require a form that can refer to the data in a table or query and can additionally display data from another table, you should create a subform. \</variable\> For example, this subform can be a text box that displays the data of another database table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157972				0	ca-XR	A subform is an additional component of the main form. The main form can be called the "parent form" or "master". Subforms are needed as soon as you want to access more than one table from a form. Each additional table requires its own subform.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id4807275				0	ca-XR	After creating a form, it can be changed into a subform. To do this, enter Design Mode, and open the Form Navigator. In the Form Navigator, drag a form (that will become a subform) onto any other form (that will become a master).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	ca-XR	The user of your document will not see that a form has subforms. The user only sees a document in which data is entered or where existing data is displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2A				0	ca-XR	Specify the Link master field from the data fields in the master form. In the subform, the Link slave field can be set as a field which will be matched to the contents of the Link master field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2D				0	ca-XR	When the user navigates through the data, the form always displays the current data record. If there are subforms defined, the contents of the subforms will be displayed after a short delay of approximate 200 ms. This delay enables you to quickly browse through the data records of the master form. If you navigate to the next master data record within the delay limit, the subform data need not be retrieved and displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Internet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070100.xhp\" name=\"Internet\"\>Internet\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230				0	ca-XR	Use the \<emph\>Internet\</emph\> page of the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> to edit hyperlinks with WWW or FTP addresses.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147291				0	ca-XR	The fields for the login name, password and anonymous user are only available for FTP addresses.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145090				0	ca-XR	Type of hyperlink				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151226				0	ca-XR	Web				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_INTERNET:RB_LINKTYP_INTERNET\"\>Creates an http hyperlink.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153683				0	ca-XR	FTP				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_INTERNET:RB_LINKTYP_FTP\"\>Creates an FTP hyperlink.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149095				0	ca-XR	Telnet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:RADIOBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_INTERNET:RB_LINKTYP_TELNET\"\>Creates a Telnet hyperlink.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150443				0	ca-XR	Target				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id9887081				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter a URL for the file that you want to open when you click the hyperlink. If you do not specify a target frame, the file opens in the current document or frame.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	ca-XR	WWW Browser				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153760				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:IMAGEBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_INTERNET:BTN_BROWSE\"\>Opens a web browser, into which you can load the desired URL.\</ahelp\> You can then copy and paste the URL into the \<emph\>Target\</emph\> field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155421				0	ca-XR	Target in document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:IMAGEBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_INTERNET:BTN_TARGET\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Target in Document\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\> There you can select the destination within a document and add it to the target URL with the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HYPERLINK_MARKWND_TREE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the position in the target document where you wish to jump to.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HYPERLINK_MARKWND_APPLY\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts the target in the \<emph\>Target\</emph\> field of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HYPERLINK_MARKWND_CLOSE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Once the hyperlink has been completely entered, click on \<emph\>Close\</emph\> to set the link and leave the dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153320				0	ca-XR	Login name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_HYPERLINK_INTERNET:ED_LOGIN\"\>Specifies your login name, if you are working with FTP addresses.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\09070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148944				0	ca-XR	Password				20200411 15:09:53
