helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	General				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153681				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"General\"\>General\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233	2			0	ca-XR	This \<emph\>General \</emph\>tab enables you to define the general properties of a form control. These properties differ, depending on the control type. Not all of the following properties are available for every control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155342				0	ca-XR	If you export the current form document to HTML format, the default control values are exported, not the current control values. Default values are determined - depending on the type of control - by the properties' Default value (for example, in text fields), Default status (for check boxes and option fields), and Default selection (for list boxes).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149734				0	ca-XR	Enabled				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ENABLED\"\>If a control field has the property "Enabled" (Yes), the form user will be able to use the control field.\</ahelp\> If the property is disabled, it will not be enabled (No) and will be displayed in a gray color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153320				0	ca-XR	Line count				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149235	75			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_LINECOUNT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies how many lines should be displayed in the dropdown list. This setting is only active if you chose "Yes" in the "Dropdown" option.\</ahelp\>For combo boxes with the Dropdown property, you can specify how many lines should be displayed in the dropdown list. With control fields which do not have the Dropdown option, the line's display will be specified by the size of the control field and the font size.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153147				0	ca-XR	Action				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415	24			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_BUTTONTYPE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The Action property determines the action that occurs when you activate a button.\</ahelp\>You can use navigation actions to design your own database navigation buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152474				0	ca-XR	The following table describes the actions that you can assign to a button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	ca-XR	Action				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154388				0	ca-XR	Description				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154071				0	ca-XR	None				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153797				0	ca-XR	No action occurs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	ca-XR	Submit form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228	31			0	ca-XR	Sends the data that is entered in other control fields of the current form to the address that is specified in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170200.xhp\" name=\"Form Properties\"\>Form Properties\</link\> under \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170201.xhp\" name=\"URL\"\>\<emph\>URL\</emph\>\</link\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F7				0	ca-XR	Enter the URL into the form's data property "URL" text box when you export to a PDF file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	ca-XR	Reset form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155101				0	ca-XR	Resets the settings in other control fields to the predefined defaults (Default Status, Default Selection, Default Value).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155431				0	ca-XR	Open document / web page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	ca-XR	Opens the URL that is specified under \<emph\>URL\</emph\>. You can use \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> to specify the target frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	ca-XR	First record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10803				0	ca-XR	Moves the current form to the first record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	ca-XR	Previous record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1080E				0	ca-XR	Moves the current form to the previous record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	ca-XR	Next record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10819				0	ca-XR	Moves the current form to the next record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081F				0	ca-XR	Last record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	ca-XR	Moves the current form to the last record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	ca-XR	Save record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	ca-XR	Saves the current record, if necessary.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10835				0	ca-XR	Undo data entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083A				0	ca-XR	Reverses the changes in the current record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10840				0	ca-XR	New record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	ca-XR	Moves the current form to the insert row.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084B				0	ca-XR	Delete record				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10850				0	ca-XR	Deletes the current record.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN10856				0	ca-XR	Refresh form				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085B				0	ca-XR	Reloads the most recently saved version of the current form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154638				0	ca-XR	Dropdown				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577	20			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DROPDOWN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies whether the combo box should dropdown (Yes) or not (No).\</ahelp\>A control field with the dropdown property has an additional arrow button which opens the list of the existing form entries per mouse click. Under \<emph\>Line count\</emph\>, you can specify how many lines (or rows) should be displayed in the dropdown state. Combination fields can have the dropdown property.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3159198				0	ca-XR	Combo boxes that were inserted as columns in a table control are always dropdown as the default.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153140				0	ca-XR	Alignment / Graphics alignment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151281	12			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALIGN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the alignment option for text or graphics that are used on a control.\</ahelp\>The alignment options are left-aligned, right-aligned, and centered. These options are available for the following elements:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109DD				0	ca-XR	Title of Label fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E1				0	ca-XR	Content of text fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E5				0	ca-XR	Content of table fields in the columns of a table control				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E9				0	ca-XR	Graphics or text that are used in buttons				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	ca-XR	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> option for buttons is called \<emph\>Graphics alignment\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153141				0	ca-XR	Vertical Alignment				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151394				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_VERTICAL_ALIGN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Specifies the vertical alignment for text or graphics content which used on a control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151073				0	ca-XR	AutoFill				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152375	77			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_AUTOCOMPLETE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Assigns the AutoFill function to a combo box.\</ahelp\>The AutoFill function displays a list of previous entries after you start to type an entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	ca-XR	Label field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CONTROLLABEL\"\>Specifies the source for the label of the control.\</ahelp\> The text of the label field will be used instead of the name of a database field. For example, in the \<emph\>Filter Navigator\</emph\>, \<emph\>Search\</emph\> dialog, and as a column name in the table view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	ca-XR	To define one character of the label as a mnemonic, so that the user can access this control by pressing the character on the keyboard, insert a tilde (~) character in front of the character in the label.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154502				0	ca-XR	Only the text of a group frame can be used as the label field when using radio buttons. This text applies to all of the radio buttons of the same group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148587				0	ca-XR	If you click on the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button next to the text field, you will see the \<emph\>Label Field Selection\</emph\> dialog. Select a label from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154512	220			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"PCR_CHECKBOX_RID_DLG_SELECTLABELCONTROL_1\"\>Check the \<emph\>No assignment \</emph\>box to remove the link between a control and the assigned label field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148834				0	ca-XR	Width				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148566	143			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_WIDTH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the column width in the table control field.\</ahelp\>Sets the column width in the table control field in the units that are specified in the %PRODUCTNAME module options. If you want, you can enter a value followed by a valid measurement unit, for example, 2 cm.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877803				0	ca-XR	Repeat				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id9863277				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REPEAT\"\>Specifies if the action of a control such as a spin button repeats when you click the control and hold the mouse button down.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id9827875				0	ca-XR	Delay				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id6092715				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_REPEAT_DELAY\"\>Specifies the delay in milliseconds between repeating events.\</ahelp\> A repeating event occurs when you click an arrow button or the background of a scrollbar, or one of the record navigation buttons of a Navigation Bar, and you keep the mouse button pressed for some time. You can enter a value followed by a valid time unit, for example, 2 s or 500 ms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145164				0	ca-XR	Record marker				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3147257				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_RECORDMARKER\"\>Specifies whether the first column is displayed with row labels, in which the current record is marked by an arrow.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151019				0	ca-XR	Date format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971	83			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATEFORMAT\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Here, you can determine the format you want for the date readout.\</ahelp\>With date fields you can determine the format for the date readout.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151356				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"hinweis\"\>All format fields (date, time, currency, numeric) are formatted automatically in the selected format as soon as you leave them regardless of how you entered the input.\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156054				0	ca-XR	Spin Button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360	88			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SPIN\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The "Yes" option transforms the control field into a spin button, where corresponding arrow buttons are added.\</ahelp\>Numerical fields, currency fields, date and time fields can be introduced as spin buttons in the form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159268				0	ca-XR	Tristate				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_TRISTATE\"\>Specifies whether a check box can also represent ZERO values of a linked database apart from the TRUE and FALSE values.\</ahelp\> This function is only available if the database accepts three states: TRUE, FALSE and ZERO.				20200411 15:09:53
