helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154142				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>form controls;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; form fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>form fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>command button creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>push buttons;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>radio button creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>check box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>labels; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fixed text; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text boxes;form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>list box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>picklist creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drop-down lists in form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combo box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; select mode\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154142				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Form Controls\"\>Form Controls\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151378				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"formulartext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Config\"\>The Form Controls toolbar contains tools that you need to create an interactive form.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can use the toolbar to add controls to a form in a text, spreadsheet, presentation, or HTML document, for example a button that runs a macro.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200809391346				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	ca-XR	Icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar (you may need to enable this initially invisible icon):				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3150943\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_config.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150943\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	ca-XR	Form Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B21				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xforms.xhp\"\>XML Form documents\</link\> (XForms) use the same controls.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152771				0	ca-XR	To create a form, open a document and use the Form Controls toolbar to add and define the form controls. If you want, you can also link the form to a database, so that you can use the controls to manipulate a database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791				0	ca-XR	When you create a form in an HTML document, you can use the form to send data over the Internet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	ca-XR	%PRODUCTNAME only exports the form properties that are supported by the HTML version that you export to. To specify the HTML version, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C39				0	ca-XR	To add a control to a document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	ca-XR	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the icon of the control that you want to add.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C4D				0	ca-XR	In the document, drag to create the control. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C50				0	ca-XR	To create a square control field, hold down the Shift key while you drag.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127				0	ca-XR	To add a field from the field list of a table or query to a form, drag a cell into the form. In a text document, you can also drag a column header to add a field to a form. To include a label for the field, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift key down when you drag a column head.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C87				0	ca-XR	Modifying a Control				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	ca-XR	Right-click the control and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>. A dialog opens where you can define the properties of the control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	ca-XR	To specify a accelerator key for a control, add a tilde (~) in front of the character in the label for the control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152792	135			0	ca-XR	You can drag and drop controls from one document to another document. You can also copy and paste controls between documents. When you insert a control from another document, $[officename] analyzes the data source, content type, and content properties of the control so that the control fits the logical structure in the target document. For example, a control that displays contents from an address book continues to display the same contents after you copy the control to a different document. You can view these properties on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of the \<emph\>Form properties\</emph\> dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154411				0	ca-XR	Select				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3153516\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153516\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150470				0	ca-XR	This icon switches the mouse pointer to the select mode, or deactivates this mode. The select mode is used to select the controls of the current form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146914				0	ca-XR	Check Box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148483				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3156380\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_checkbox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156380\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CheckBox\"\>Creates a check box.\</ahelp\> Check boxes allow you to activate or deactivate a function in a form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794				0	ca-XR	Text Box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3153266\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_edit.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153266\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Edit\"\>Creates a text box.\</ahelp\> Text boxes are fields in which the user can enter text. In a form, text boxes display data or allow for new data input.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151218				0	ca-XR	Formatted Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154836				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3143277\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formattedfield.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143277\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147547				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormattedField\"\>Creates a formatted field.\</ahelp\> A formatted field is a text box in which you can define how the inputs and outputs are formatted, and which limiting values apply.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155346				0	ca-XR	A formatted field has \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170002.xhp\" name=\"special control properties\"\>special control properties\</link\> (choose \<emph\>Format - Control\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148774				0	ca-XR	Push Button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3151073\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertpushbutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151073\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147046				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pushbutton\"\>Creates a push button.\</ahelp\> This function can be used to execute a command for a defined event, such as a mouse click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	ca-XR	You can apply text and graphics to these buttons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157844				0	ca-XR	Option Button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3152999\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_radiobutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152999\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RadioButton\"\>Creates an option button.\</ahelp\> Option buttons enable the user to choose one of several options. Option buttons with the same functionality are given the same name (\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Name\"\>\<emph\>Name\</emph\>\</link\>\<emph\>property\</emph\>). Normally, they are given a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"group box\"\>group box\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156064				0	ca-XR	List Box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3154135\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_listbox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154135\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ListBox\"\>Creates a list box.\</ahelp\> A list box lets users select an entry from a list. If the form is linked to a database and the database connection is active, the\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"List Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after the list box is inserted in the document. This wizard helps you create the list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171				0	ca-XR	Combo Box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3148817\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_combobox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148817\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149407				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ComboBox\"\>Creates a combo box.\</ahelp\> A combo box is a single-line list box with a drop-down list from which users choose an option. You can assign the "read-only" property to the combo box so that users cannot enter other entries than those found in the list. If the form is bound to a database and the database connection is active, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after you insert the combo box in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145618				0	ca-XR	Label Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3151017\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfixedtext.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151017\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Label\"\>Creates a field for displaying text.\</ahelp\> These labels are only for displaying predefined text. Entries cannot be made in these fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	ca-XR	More Controls				20200411 15:09:53
