helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Conversion of measurement units				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147543				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>measurement units; converting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>units; converting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;metrics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>metrics;converting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147543				0	ca-XR	Conversion of measurement units				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069F				0	ca-XR	In some dialogs, you can enter measurement values into input boxes. If you just enter a numerical value, the default measurement unit is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A2				0	ca-XR	You define the default measurement unit for Writer text documents in the dialog that you get by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</emph\>. For Calc, Draw, and Impress, you open a document of that type and then open the appropriate \<emph\>General\</emph\> page as for Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AD				0	ca-XR	In input boxes for length units you can also add the unit abbreviation according to the following list:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	ca-XR	Unit abbreviation				20200411 15:09:53
