helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389				0	ca-XR	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Changing Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	ca-XR	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	ca-XR	Modifying Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	ca-XR	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	ca-XR	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	ca-XR	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	ca-XR	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	ca-XR	Resetting Default Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	ca-XR	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	ca-XR	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	ca-XR	Using Custom Templates				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	ca-XR	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	ca-XR	Templates in the Template Folder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	ca-XR	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialog. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	ca-XR	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	ca-XR	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Assistive Tools in $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	ca-XR	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id8847010				0	ca-XR	A current list of supported assistive tools can be found on the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\"\>Apache OpenOffice Wiki\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	ca-XR	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	ca-XR	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	ca-XR	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	ca-XR	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	ca-XR	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795				0	ca-XR	Supported Assistive Tools				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	ca-XR	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	ca-XR	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	ca-XR	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	ca-XR	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	ca-XR	Supported Input Devices				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	ca-XR	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	ca-XR	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	ca-XR	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	ca-XR	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808				0	ca-XR	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	ca-XR	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010800.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - View\"\>$[officename] - View\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155430				0	ca-XR	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Appearance\"\>$[officename] - Appearance\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148617				0	ca-XR	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Accessibility\"\>$[officename] - Accessibility\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
