helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154824				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"data_dbase2office\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_dbase2office.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	ca-XR	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBASE import and export, you can use a common text format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	ca-XR	Importing Data into $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	ca-XR	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	ca-XR	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	ca-XR	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
