helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	ca-XR	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	ca-XR	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	ca-XR	In the document, drag to draw the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	ca-XR	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	ca-XR	Specify the properties of the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	ca-XR	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	ca-XR	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
