helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	hd_id4989165				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_receive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	ca-XR	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can open and save documents that are stored on a WebDAV server, using the secure HTTPS protocol.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	ca-XR	You must use the %PRODUCTNAME file dialogs to use WebDAV over HTTPS.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	ca-XR	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\>. Ensure that \<emph\>Use %PRODUCTNAME dialogs\</emph\> is enabled. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7424237				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter the path to the WebDAV folder. For example, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>https://192.168.1.1/webfolder\</item\> to open a secure connection to the WebDAV server at the IP address 192.168.1.1, and to list the contents of the \<item type=\"literal\"\>webfolder\</item\> folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	ca-XR	The first time you connect to a WebDAV server, you see the "\<emph\>Website Certified by an Unknown Authority\</emph\>" dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	ca-XR	You should click the \<emph\>Examine Certificate\</emph\> button and examine the certificate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	ca-XR	If you accept the certificate, choose "\<emph\>Accept this certificate temporarily for this session\</emph\>" and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Now you can open and save files from the WebDAV server without further questions, until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	ca-XR	If you do not trust the certificate, click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	ca-XR	If you did accept the certificate, you can now select the file name or file names you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	ca-XR	If there is a mismatch of the domain name given in the certificate and the domain name you entered in the file dialog, then you see a dialog that allows you to choose from any of the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	ca-XR	 \<emph\>View Certificate\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	ca-XR	 \<emph\>Continue\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you are sure both domains are the same, click the Continue button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	ca-XR	 \<emph\>Cancel Connection\</emph\> - Cancels the connection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	ca-XR	If you click \<emph\>Continue\</emph\>, you may see a dialog that asks you to enter your user name and password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name to log on to the WebDAV server.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your password.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If you enable \<emph\>Remember password till end of session\</emph\>, your password will be remembered for subsequent WebDAV connections until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3204443				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/How_to_use_digital_Signatures\"\>English Wiki page on digital signatures\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
