helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	ca-XR	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#ctl\" name=\"CTL languages\"\>CTL languages\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3155420				0	ca-XR	If you select the text flow from right to left, embedded Western text still runs from left to right. The cursor responds to the arrow keys in that Right Arrow moves it "to the text end" and Left Arrow "to the text start".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	ca-XR	You can change the text writing direction directly be pressing one of the following keys:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	ca-XR	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+D or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Right Shift Key - switch to right-to-left text entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	ca-XR	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+A or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Left Shift Key - switch to left-to-right text entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	ca-XR	The modifier-only key combinations only work when CTL support is enabled.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	ca-XR	In multicolumn pages, sections or frames that are formatted with text flow from right to left, the first column is the right column and the last column is the left column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	ca-XR	In $[officename] Writer text formatted in \<emph\>Thai language\</emph\> has the following features:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ca-XR	In paragraphs with justified alignment, the characters are stretched to flush the lines at the margins. In other languages the spaces between words are stretched.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	ca-XR	Use the Delete key to delete a whole composite character. Use the Backspace key to delete the last part of the previous composite character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809				0	ca-XR	Use the Right or Left Arrow key to jump to the next or previous whole composite character. To position the cursor into a composite character, use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
