helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3154897				0	ca-XR	Working in $[officename], you can send the current document as an e-mail attachment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Document as E-mail\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	ca-XR	$[officename] opens your default e-mail program.\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\> If you want to send the current document with another e-mail program, you can select the program to use with \<emph\>Internet - E-mail\</emph\> in the Options dialog box.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	ca-XR	In your e-mail program, enter the recipient, subject and any text you want to add, then send the e-mail.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\email.xhp	0	help	par_id3595385				0	ca-XR	In case you want to send the e-mail to a recipient who only has software that cannot read the OpenDocument format, you can send the current document in an often used proprietary format.\<br/\>For a text document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Word\</item\>. For a spreadsheet, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft Excel\</item\>. And for a presentation, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as Microsoft PowerPoint\</item\>. \<br/\>If you want to send the document as a read-only file, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Send - Document as PDF\</item\>.\<br/\>These commands do not change your current document. Only a temporary copy is created and sent.				20200411 15:09:53
