helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	ca-XR	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F10.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479				0	ca-XR	Selecting objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993				0	ca-XR	Press Shift+F4 to select the first object in the current document. When an object is selected, press Tab to select the next object, or press Esc to go back to the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152962				0	ca-XR	Edit Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156379				0	ca-XR	A selected OLE object can be activated with the Enter key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	ca-XR	Edit Position and Size of Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	ca-XR	Use the arrow keys to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145619				0	ca-XR	Set the grid resolution unit with \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> area. If you enter a number greater than 1 in the \<emph\>Subdivision\</emph\> area, you must press the arrow key as often as the number states to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	ca-XR	Use the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and arrow keys to move the selected object by one pixel.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	ca-XR	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to enter the handle edit mode. The upper left handle is the active handle, it starts blinking. Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to select the next handle. Press Escape to exit the handle edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	ca-XR	In the handle edit mode, the arrow keys move the selected handle, which changes the object size.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	ca-XR	Edit the Anchors of Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534				0	ca-XR	You can move the anchor of an object with the arrow keys. First enter the handle edit mode and select the anchor. Depending on the type of anchor, you can then move the anchor in different directions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	ca-XR	Select the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646				0	ca-XR	Enter the handle edit mode with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	ca-XR	The upper left handle starts blinking. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab several times, until no handle blinks. This signals that now the anchor of the object is activated. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In text documents you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A to activate the anchor directly.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	ca-XR	Use the arrow keys to move the anchor. The object follows the anchor as appropriate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	ca-XR	You can change the anchor of the selected object for example in the object's context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148393				0	ca-XR	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To Paragraph\</emph\>, the arrow keys move the object to the previous or next paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615	69			0	ca-XR	If the object is anchored\<emph\> To page\</emph\>, the keys Page Up or Page Down move it to the previous or next page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135				0	ca-XR	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To character\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it through the current paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256	71			0	ca-XR	If the object is anchored\<emph\> As character\</emph\>, no anchor icon exists. You cannot move the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149527				0	ca-XR	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To frame\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it to the next frame in the respective direction.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153270				0	ca-XR	Controlling the Dividing Lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413	134			0	ca-XR	Documents of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw, and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress can be split horizontally and vertically into separate views. Each view can show other parts of the document. Using the mouse, you can drag a dividing line from the scrollbar into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	ca-XR	Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6: shows the dividing lines at default positions and focus a line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	ca-XR	Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a big step in the arrow direction.				20200411 15:09:53
