helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	ca-XR	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	ca-XR	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	ca-XR	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	ca-XR	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	ca-XR	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				20200411 15:09:53
