helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153575				0	ca-XR	Save URLs relative to file system				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	ca-XR	This option allows you to select the default for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#speichern\" name=\"relative\"\>relative\</link\> addressing of URLs in the file system and on the Internet. Relative addressing is only possible if the source document and the referenced document are both on the same drive.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	ca-XR	A relative address always starts from the directory in which the current document is located. In contrast, absolute addressing always starts from a root directory. The following table demonstrates the difference in syntax between relative and absolute referencing:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149413				0	ca-XR	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
