helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	ca-XR	Defines the settings for the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#proxy\" name=\"proxy server\"\>proxy server\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151110				0	ca-XR	Proxy server				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:LB_PROXYMODE\"\>Specifies the type of proxy definition.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	ca-XR	None				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ca-XR	Accesses the Internet without a proxy server. Allows you to set up a connection directly on your computer to an Internet provider that does not use a proxy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150984				0	ca-XR	Manual				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	ca-XR	Lets you enter the proxy server manually. Specify the proxy servers in accordance with your Internet service. Ask your system administrator for the proxies and ports to enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	ca-XR	Type server names without the protocol prefix. For example, type www.example.com, not http://www.example.com.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10684				0	ca-XR	System				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10688				0	ca-XR	On Windows or UNIX systems using GNOME or KDE, this option tells %PRODUCTNAME to use the system settings. You must restart %PRODUCTNAME to initiate this setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148948				0	ca-XR	HTTP proxy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_HTTP_PROXY\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#http\" name=\"HTTP\"\>HTTP\</link\>.\</ahelp\> Type the port in the right-hand field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id9971922				0	ca-XR	HTTPS proxy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id5319071				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for HTTPS. Type the port in the right-hand field.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150543				0	ca-XR	FTP proxy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_EDIT_RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY_ED_FTP_PROXY\"\>Type the name of the proxy server for \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#ftp\" name=\"FTP\"\>FTP\</link\>.\</ahelp\> Type the port in the right-hand field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	ca-XR	No proxy for				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151178				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_PROXY:ED_NOPROXYFOR\"\>Specifies the names of the servers that do not require any proxy servers, separated by semicolons.\</ahelp\> These are servers addressed in your local network, and servers used for video and audio streaming, for example.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	ca-XR	You can also use placeholders for the names of hosts and domains. For example, type *.sun.com to address all the hosts in the sun.com domain without proxy.				20200411 15:09:53
