helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2F				0	ca-XR	Specifies the properties for the current paragraph or the selected paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3A				0	ca-XR	Merge with next paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"svx:CheckBox:RID_SVXPAGE_BORDER:CB_MERGEWITHNEXT\"\>Merges the border style and the shadow style of the current paragraph with the next paragraph.\</ahelp\> These styles are only merged if the indent, border, and shadow styles of the next paragraph are the same as the current paragraph. This option is also available for Paragraph Styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BA				0	ca-XR	Merge adjacent line styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BE				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"700793922\"\>Merges two different border styles of adjacent cells in a Writer table into one border style. This property is valid for a whole table in a Writer document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05030500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C1				0	ca-XR	The rules can be condensed to the statement that the stronger attribute wins. If, for example, one cell has a red border of 2 point width, and the adjacent cell has a blue border of 3 point width, then the common border between these two cells will be blue with 3 point width.				20200411 15:09:53
