helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS\"\>Specify the font effects that you want to use.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149482				0	ca-XR	Font Color				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146924				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXPAGE_CHAR_EFFECTS_LB_FONTCOLOR\"\>Sets the color for the selected text. If you select\<emph\> Automatic\</emph\>, the text color is set to black for light backgrounds and to white for dark backgrounds.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC2				0	ca-XR	To change the color of a text selection, select the text that you want to change, and click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC9				0	ca-XR	If you click the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon before you select text, the paint can cursor appears. To change the color of text, select the text with the paint can cursor. To change the color of a single word, double-click in a word. To apply a different color, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Font Color\</emph\> icon, and then select the color that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CD6				0	ca-XR	To undo the last change, right-click.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDA				0	ca-XR	To exit the paint can mode, click once, or press the Escape key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150037				0	ca-XR	The text color is ignored when printing, if the \<emph\>Print black\</emph\> check box is selected in \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040400.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Print\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>\</link\> in the Options dialog box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id7613757				0	ca-XR	The text color is ignored on screen, if the \<emph\>Use automatic font color for screen display\</emph\> check box is selected in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01013000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Accessibility\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3144766				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FontColor\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>\<variable id=\"textfarbe\"\>Click to apply the current font color to the selected characters. You can also click here, and then drag a selection to change the text color. Click the arrow next to the icon to open the Font color toolbar.\</variable\>\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146137				0	ca-XR	Effects				20200411 15:09:53
