helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/11080000.xhp\" name=\"Execute SQL statement\"\>Execute SQL statement\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154288				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"sqltext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens a dialog where you can enter an SQL command for administering a database.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	ca-XR	You can only enter administration commands in this dialog, such as Grant, Create Table, or Drop Table, and not filter commands. The commands that you can enter depend on the data source, for example, dBASE can only run some of the SQL commands list here.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860				0	ca-XR	To run an SQL query for filtering data in the database, use the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design View\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149514				0	ca-XR	Command to execute				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_DIRECTSQL_ME_SQL\"\>Enter the SQL administration command that you want to run.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	ca-XR	For example, for a "Bibliography" data source, you can enter the following SQL command:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	ca-XR	SELECT "Address" FROM "biblio" "biblio"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145611				0	ca-XR	For more information on SQL commands, please consult the documentation that came with the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	ca-XR	Previous commands				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_DIRECTSQL_LB_HISTORY\"\>Lists the previously executed SQL commands. To run a command again, click the command, and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154348				0	ca-XR	Status				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\11080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_MULTILINEEDIT_DLG_DIRECTSQL_ME_STATUS\"\>Displays the results, including errors, of the SQL command that you ran.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
