helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Data Point				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Data Point\"\>Data Point\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	ca-XR	This dialog allows you to change the properties of a selected data point. The dialog appears when there is only one data point selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Format Selection\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149121				0	ca-XR	Any changes made only affect this one data point. For example, if you edit the color of a bar, only the color of that bar will be different.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	3D View 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>3D charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; 3D views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Illumination; 3D charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3464461				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"three_d_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	ca-XR	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> or in the context menu of a chart you can choose a chart type. \<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog to edit the properties of a three dimensional view for Column, Bar, Pie, and Area charts. For Line and XY (Scatter) charts you can see 3D lines.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	ca-XR	The chart preview responds to the new settings that you enter in the dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	ca-XR	When you leave the dialog with OK, the settings are applied permanently. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	ca-XR	When you leave the dialog with Cancel or Escape, the chart returns to the state when you opened the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8081911				0	ca-XR	For a 3D chart you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - 3D View\</item\> to set perspective, appearance and illumination.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id2924283				0	ca-XR	Perspective				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	ca-XR	Enter the values for rotation of the chart on the three axes and for a perspective view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9999694				0	ca-XR	Set all angles to 0 for a front view of the chart. Pie charts and donut charts are shown as circles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2861720				0	ca-XR	With Right-angled axes enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	ca-XR	An x value of 90, with y and z set to 0, provides a view from top down to the chart. With x set to -90, you see the bottom of the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	ca-XR	The rotations are applied in the order first x, then y, last z.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	ca-XR	When shading is enabled and you rotate a chart, the lights are rotated as if they are fixed to the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2578203				0	ca-XR	The rotation axes always relate to the page, not to the chart's axes. This is different from some other chart programs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4923245				0	ca-XR	Select the Perspective check box to view the chart in central perspective as through a camera lens instead of using a parallel projection. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3416547				0	ca-XR	Set the focus length with the spin button. 100% gives a perspective view where a far edge in the chart looks approximately half as big as a near edge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	ca-XR	Older versions of %PRODUCTNAME cannot display the percentage of perspective the same way as the current version.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7623828				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Right-angled axes is enabled, you can rotate the chart contents only in X and Y direction, that is, parallel to the chart borders. Right-angled axes is enabled by default for newly created 3D charts. Pie and Donut charts do not support right-angled axes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the x axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the y axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8915372				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Sets the rotation of the chart on the z axis. The preview responds to the new settings.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6070436				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Mark the Perspective box to view the chart as through a camera lens. Use the spin button to set the percentage. With a high percentage nearer objects look bigger than more distant objects.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id7564012				0	ca-XR	Appearance				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1186254				0	ca-XR	Select a scheme from the list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7432477				0	ca-XR	By selecting a scheme, the check boxes and the light sources are set accordingly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7141026				0	ca-XR	If you mark or unmark a combination of check boxes that is not given by the Realistic or Simple scheme, you create a Custom scheme.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id1579027				0	ca-XR	Mark \<emph\>Shading\</emph\> to use the Gouraud method for rendering the surface, otherwise a flat method is used. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5624561				0	ca-XR	The flat method sets a single color and brightness for each polygon. The edges are visible, soft gradients and spot lights are not possible. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id5901058				0	ca-XR	The Gouraud method applies gradients for a smoother, more realistic look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8469191				0	ca-XR	Mark \<emph\>Object Borders\</emph\> to draw lines along the edges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id4407483				0	ca-XR	Mark \<emph\>Rounded Edges\</emph\> to smooth the edges of box shapes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id8531449				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a scheme from the list box, or click any of the check boxes below.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Applies Gouraud shading if marked, or flat shading if unmarked.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Shows borders around the areas by setting the line style to Solid.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Edges are rounded by 5%.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id1939451				0	ca-XR	Illumination				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	ca-XR	Set the light sources for the 3D view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6531266				0	ca-XR	Click any of the eight buttons to switch a directed light source on or off.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6173894				0	ca-XR	By default, the second light source is switched on. It is the first of seven "normal", uniform light sources. The light source number one projects a specular light with highlights.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	ca-XR	For the selected light source, you can then choose a color and intensity in the list box just below the eight buttons. The brightness values of all lights are added, so use dark colors when you enable multiple lights.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	ca-XR	The small preview inside this tab page has two sliders to set the vertical and horizontal position of the selected light source. The light source always aims to the middle of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	ca-XR	The button in the corner of the small preview switches the internal illumination model between a sphere and a cube.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	ca-XR	Use the Ambient light list box to define the ambient light which shines with a uniform intensity from all directions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the right slider to set the vertical height and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Drag the bottom slider to set the horizontal position and direction of the selected light source.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to switch between an illumination model of a sphere or a cube.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id533768				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the specular light source with highlights.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\three_d_view.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to enable or disable the uniform light source.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
