helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8829309				0	ca-XR	On this page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can select one single source of data range. This range may consist of more than one rectangular range of cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Data Ranges dialog where you can edit Data Range and Data Series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2025818				0	ca-XR	Use the Chart Wizard - Data Series page if you need more control over the data ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id8466139				0	ca-XR	This dialog is only available for charts based on a Calc or Writer table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	hd_id1877193				0	ca-XR	To specify a data range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5924863				0	ca-XR	Select the data range. Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4357432				0	ca-XR	Enter the data range in the text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5626392				0	ca-XR	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1363872				0	ca-XR	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog, then drag over a cell area to select the data range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id6823938				0	ca-XR	If you want a data range of multiple cell areas that are not next to each other, enter the first range, then manually add a semicolon at the end of the text box, then enter the other ranges. Use a semicolon as delimiter between ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id1434369				0	ca-XR	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	ca-XR	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	ca-XR	In the preview you can see how the final chart will look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id379650				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the data range that you want to include in your chart. To minimize this dialog while you select the data range in Calc, click the \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id953703				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive rows in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data series will contain x-values for all series. All other data series are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id4496597				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Data series get their data from consecutive columns in the selected range. For scatter charts, the first data column will contain x-values for all series. All other data columns are used as y-values, one for each series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id2898953				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first row in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first row in the range is used as categories. The remaining rows comprise the data series. If this check box is not selected, all rows are data series.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_data_range.xhp	0	help	par_id7546311				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>For data series in columns: The first column in the range is used as names for data series. For data series in rows: The first column in the range is used as categories. The remaining columns comprise the data columns. If this check box is not selected, all columns are data columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Arrangement				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Arrangement\"\>Arrangement\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	ca-XR	Allows you to modify the order of the data series already set in the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411				0	ca-XR	The position of the data in the data table remains unchanged. You can only choose the commands after inserting a chart in $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	ca-XR	This function is only available if you have data displayed in columns. It is not possible to switch to data display in rows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147339				0	ca-XR	Bring Forward				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149259				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Forward\"\>Brings the selected data series forward (to the right).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146316				0	ca-XR	Send Backward				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05120000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Backward\"\>Sends the selected data series backward (to the left).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Chart Area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149670				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>charts; formatting areas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; chart areas\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149670				0	ca-XR	Chart Area				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	2			0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"diagrammflaeche\"\>\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\".uno:DiagramArea\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Chart Area\</emph\> dialog, where you can modify the properties of the chart area. The chart area is the background behind all elements of the chart.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Chart Type Stock				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	bm_id2959990				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>stock charts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chart types;stock\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data sources;setting for stock charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id966216				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"type_stock\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_stock.xhp\"\>Chart Type Stock\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3516953				0	ca-XR	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5268410				0	ca-XR	Stock				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id61342				0	ca-XR	A Stock chart illustrates the market trend given by opening price, bottom price, top price and closing price. The transaction volume can also be shown.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2131412				0	ca-XR	For a Stock chart the order of the data series is important. The data should be arranged as shown in the example table below.				20200411 15:09:53
