helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149871				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>colors; default colors\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871				0	ca-XR	The CMYK list is optimized for print colors, whereas the colors in the Web and the HTML lists are optimized for displays using a resolution of 256 colors.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150435				0	ca-XR	To load a gradient list:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3150393				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3146322				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Load Gradients List\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946				0	ca-XR	Locate the gradient list that you want to load, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. A gradient list file has the format [filename].sog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	ca-XR	To save a gradients list, click the \<emph\>Save Gradients List\</emph\> button, enter a filename, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\palette_files.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153036				0	ca-XR	To load a hatching list:				20200411 15:09:53
