helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1356547				0	ca-XR	Every slide is based on a slide master. The text, pictures, tables, fields or other objects that you place on the slide master are visible as a background on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id704672				0	ca-XR	Masters exist for slides, notes, and handouts. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8403576				0	ca-XR	To edit a slide master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5641651				0	ca-XR	To edit a notes master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Notes Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the notes master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1583300				0	ca-XR	To edit a handout master, click the Handout tab above the slide. Click the Normal tab to leave the handout master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id7251808				0	ca-XR	Adding predefined header or footer objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5015411				0	ca-XR	Every type of master has some predefined areas to hold the date, footer, and slide numbers. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8217413				0	ca-XR	When you switch to the master view, you can move that areas to any position on the master. You can enter additional text and resize the areas. You can select the contents of the areas and apply text formats. For example, you can change the font size or color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id7549668				0	ca-XR	A predefined Header Area is available only for notes and handouts. If you want a header on all slides, you can move the Footer Area on the slide master to the top.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1829889				0	ca-XR	Objects that you insert on a slide master are visible on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8843043				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>View - Header and Footer\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1876583				0	ca-XR	You see a dialog with two tab pages: \<emph\>Slide\</emph\> and \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> where you can enter contents to the predefined areas. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id4101077				0	ca-XR	By default, the \<emph\>Date and Time\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the format is set to Fixed and the text input box is empty, so no date and time is visible on the slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id204779				0	ca-XR	By default, the \<emph\>Footer\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the text input box is empty, so no footer is visible on the slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1453901				0	ca-XR	By default, the \<emph\>Slide number\</emph\> checkbox is cleared, so no slide numbers are visible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1445966				0	ca-XR	Enter or select the contents that should be visible on all slides.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1956236				0	ca-XR	If you want to change the position and formatting of the master objects, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5259559				0	ca-XR	You see the slide master with areas near the bottom. You can move the areas , and you can select the fields and apply some formatting. You can also enter some text here which will be shown next to the fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id2521439				0	ca-XR	Click the Date Area and move the time and date field. Select the <date/time> field and apply some formatting to change the format for the date and time on all slides. The same applies to the Footer Area and the Slide Number Area.				20200411 15:09:53
