helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"animated_gif_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_gif_create.xhp\" name=\"Creating Animated GIF Images\"\>Creating Animated GIF Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	ca-XR	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor where you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	ca-XR	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250				0	ca-XR	To create an animated GIF:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	ca-XR	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose\<emph\> Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	ca-XR	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Animation Group \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	ca-XR	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	ca-XR	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	ca-XR	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration \</emph\>box (middle box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	ca-XR	Repeat the last two steps for each frame in your animation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	100			0	ca-XR	You can preview your animation by using the controls to the left of the \<emph\>Image Number \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	65			0	ca-XR	Select the number of times you want the animation sequence to repeat in the \<emph\>Loop count \</emph\>box (right box).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145421				0	ca-XR	Select an alignment option for the objects in the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154285				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D scenes; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	ca-XR	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	ca-XR	Curved object based on Bézier curves				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	ca-XR	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	ca-XR	3D object with shading and a light source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	ca-XR	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id31490481				0	ca-XR	Two types of 3D objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31472951				0	ca-XR	The Status bar displays "3D scene selected". The 3D scenes are built from objects which have dimensions in x, y, and z coordinates. Examples are the objects inserted by the 3D Objects toolbar, and rectangles, ellipses, or text that got created by the Rectangle, Ellipse, or Text icons left on the Drawing toolbar, or any Custom Shapes, and that got converted to 3D by using the context menu "Convert - To 3D". These 3D scenes can be entered (for example, by pressing F3), and the objects can be rotated in 3D. Microsoft Office doesn't know these real 3D objects. When exporting these 3D scenes to Microsoft Office formats, a snapshot of the current view will be exported as a bitmap. 3D bars in charts are of this type, too.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31506541				0	ca-XR	The Status bar displays "Shape selected". The Custom Shapes can be viewed in a 2D mode or in a 3D mode. At any time, you can switch the view between the two modes. You use the Basic Shapes, Symbol Shapes, and the following icons on the Drawing toolbar to create Custom Shapes. The Custom Shapes can be changed using the 3D Settings toolbar. They do not form a 3D scene, they cannot be illuminated by more than one light source, they show no reflections, and there are some more limitations. You can convert them to a 3D scene, but then they are no longer Custom Shapes. Custom Shapes in 2D or 3D mode can be exported to and imported from Microsoft Office formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	ca-XR	To convert an object to a curved shape:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	ca-XR	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	ca-XR	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	ca-XR	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	ca-XR	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	ca-XR	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	ca-XR	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	ca-XR	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	ca-XR	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				20200411 15:09:53
