helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	ca-XR	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ca-XR	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
