helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	ca-XR	You can use the keyboard to access $[officename] Impress commands as well as to navigate through the workspace. $[officename] Impress uses the same shortcut keys as $[officename] Draw to create \<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"drawing objects\"\>drawing objects\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149602				0	ca-XR	Selecting placeholders				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	ca-XR	$[officename] Impress \<emph\>AutoLayouts\</emph\> use placeholders for slide titles, text, and objects. To select a placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>. To move to the next placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	ca-XR	If you press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> after you reach the last placeholder in a slide, a new slide is inserted after the current slide. The new slide uses the same layout as the current slide.				20200411 15:09:53
