helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button. You will now see the Basic IDE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	ca-XR	Enter the function code. In this example, we define a \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> function that calculates the volume of a rectangular solid with side lengths \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\> and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	ca-XR	Close the Basic-IDE window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	ca-XR	Your function is automatically saved in the default module and is now available. If you apply the function in a Calc document that is to be used on another computer, you can copy the function to the Calc document as described in the next section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	ca-XR	Copying a Function To a Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145232	19			0	ca-XR	In stage 2 of "Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic", in the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialog you clicked on \<emph\>Edit \</emph\>. As the default, in the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field the \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> module is selected. The \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> library resides locally in your user directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	ca-XR	If you want to copy the user-defined function to a Calc document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150086				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	ca-XR	In the Basic-IDE, select the source of your user-defined function and copy it to the clipboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081D				0	ca-XR	Close the Basic-IDE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>(Name of the Calc document) - Standard - Module1\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699				0	ca-XR	Paste the clipboard contents in the Basic-IDE of the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	ca-XR	Applying a User-defined Function in $[officename] Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148869				0	ca-XR	Once you have defined the function \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> in the Basic-IDE, you can apply it the same way as the built-in functions of $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	ca-XR	Open a Calc document and enter numbers for the function parameters \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\> in cells A1, B1, and C1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	ca-XR	Set the cursor in another cell and enter the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	ca-XR	=VOL(A1;B1;C1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3146776				0	ca-XR	The function is evaluated and you will see the result in the selected cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Importing and Exporting Text Files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; importing/exporting as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulas as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;csv files with formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	ca-XR	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	ca-XR	To Import a CSV File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	ca-XR	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	ca-XR	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	ca-XR	To Export Formulas and Values as CSV Files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	ca-XR	Click the sheet to be written as a csv file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	ca-XR	If you want to export the formulas as formulas, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200				0	ca-XR	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	ca-XR	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulas, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	ca-XR	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	ca-XR	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	ca-XR	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	ca-XR	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	ca-XR	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Text Superscript / Subscript				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>superscript text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subscript text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text super/sub\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters;superscript/subscript\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151112				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"super_subscript\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/super_subscript.xhp\" name=\"Text Superscript / Subscript\"\>Text Superscript / Subscript\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	ca-XR	In the cell, select the character that you want to put in superscript or subscript.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	ca-XR	If, for example, you want to write H20 with a subscript 2, select the 2 in the cell (not in the input line).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	ca-XR	Open the context menu for the selected character and choose \<emph\>Character\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Font Position\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	ca-XR	Select the \<emph\>Subscript\</emph\> option and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020500.xhp\" name=\"Context menu - Character - Font Position\"\>Context menu - Character - Font Position\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Automatically Calculating Series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>series; calculating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating; series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>linear series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>growth series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>powers of 2 calculations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; filling automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic cell filling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFill function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>filling;cells, automatically\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"calc_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Calculating Series\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	ca-XR	You can automatically fill cells with data with the AutoFill command or the Series command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D3				0	ca-XR	Using AutoFill				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D7				0	ca-XR	AutoFill automatically generates a data series based on a defined pattern.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	ca-XR	On a sheet, click in a cell, and type a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	ca-XR	Click in another cell and then click back in the cell where you typed the number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	ca-XR	Drag the fill handle in the bottom right corner of the cell across the cells that you want to fill, and release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	ca-XR	The cells are filled with ascending numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EE				0	ca-XR	To quickly create a list of consecutive days, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Monday\</item\> in a cell, and drag the fill handle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9720145				0	ca-XR	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	ca-XR	If you select two or more adjacent cells that contain different numbers, and drag, the remaining cells are filled with the arithmetic pattern that is recognized in the numbers. The AutoFill function also recognizes customized lists that are defined under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	ca-XR	You can double-click the fill handle to automatically fill all empty columns of the current data block. For example, first enter Jan into A1 and drag the fill handle down to A12 to get the twelve months in the first column. Now enter some values into B1 and C1. Select those two cells, and double-click the fill handle. This fills automatically the data block B1:C12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	ca-XR	Using a Defined Series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	ca-XR	Select the cell range in the sheet that you want to fill.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Fill - Series\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	ca-XR	Select the parameters for the series. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	ca-XR	If you select a \<emph\>linear\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>added\</emph\> to each consecutive number in the series to create the next value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073C				0	ca-XR	If you select a \<emph\>growth\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>multiplied\</emph\> by each consecutive number to create the next value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10747				0	ca-XR	If you select a \<emph\>date\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is added to the time unit that you specify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3159173				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Creating Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating Pivot Tables\"\>Creating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	ca-XR	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Create\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialog appears. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	ca-XR	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	ca-XR	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	ca-XR	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	ca-XR	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	ca-XR	Use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Field\</item\> dialog to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key while clicking the desired calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	ca-XR	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	ca-XR	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	ca-XR	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	ca-XR	Exit the Pivot Table dialog by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The pivot table is inserted further down.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Printing Sheet Details				20200411 15:09:53
