helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Filtering Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; filtering tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"datapilot_filtertable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_filtertable.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Pivot Tables\"\>Filtering Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ca-XR	You can use filters to remove unwanted data from a pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150441				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button in the sheet to call up the dialog for the filter conditions. Alternatively, call up the context menu of the pivot table and select the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> command. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090103.xhp\" name=\"Filter\"\>\<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Here you can filter the pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id315044199				0	ca-XR	You can also click the arrow on a button in the pivot table to show a pop-up window. In this pop-up window, you can edit the visibility settings of the associated field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344485				0	ca-XR	The pop-up window displays a list of field members associated with that field. A check box is placed to the left of each field member name. When a field has an alternative display name that differs from its original name, that name is displayed in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344449				0	ca-XR	Enable or disable a checkbox to show or hide the associated field member in the pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344493				0	ca-XR	Enable or disable the \<emph\>All\</emph\> checkbox to show all or none of the field members.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344431				0	ca-XR	Select a field member in the pop-up window and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Show only the current item\</item\> button to show only the selected field member. All other field members are hidden in the pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344484				0	ca-XR	Select a field member in the pop-up window and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide only the current item\</item\> button to hide only the selected field member. All other field members are shown in the pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344578				0	ca-XR	Commands enable you to sort the field members in ascending order, descending order, or using a custom sort list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344584				0	ca-XR	To edit the custom sort lists, open \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344811				0	ca-XR	The arrow to open the pop-up window is normally black. When the field contains one or more hidden field members, the arrow is blue and displays a tiny square at its lower-right corner.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344884				0	ca-XR	You can also open the pop-up window by positioning the cell cursor at the button and pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+D.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Changing Table Views				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147304				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>row headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views; tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids;hiding lines in sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;headers/grid lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;table views\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147304				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"table_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_view.xhp\" name=\"Changing Table Views\"\>Changing Table Views\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	ca-XR	To hide column and line headers in a table:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	ca-XR	Under the menu item \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc,\</emph\> go to the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page. Unmark\<emph\> Column/row headers\</emph\>. Confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	ca-XR	To hide grid lines:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ca-XR	Under the menu item \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>\<emph\>,\</emph\> go to the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page. Unmark \<emph\>Grid lines\</emph\>. Confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Filter: Applying Advanced Filters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148798				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>filters;defining advanced filters \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148798	18			0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"specialfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/specialfilter.xhp\" name=\"Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\"\>Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	ca-XR	Copy the column headers of the sheet ranges to be filtered into an empty area of the sheet, and then enter the criteria for the filter in a row beneath the headers. Horizontally arranged data in a row will always be logically connected with AND, and vertically arranged data in a column will always be logically connected with OR.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	ca-XR	Once you have created a filter matrix, select the sheet ranges to be filtered. Open the \<emph\>Advanced Filter\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>Data - Filter - Advanced Filter\</emph\>, and define the filter conditions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	21			0	ca-XR	Then click OK, and you will see that only the rows from the original sheet whose contents have met the search criteria are still visible. All other rows are temporarily hidden and can be made to reappear with the \<emph\>Format - Row - Show \</emph\>command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	22			0	ca-XR	 \<emph\>Example\</emph\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	ca-XR	Load a spreadsheet with a large number of records. We are using a fictional \<emph\>Turnover\</emph\> document, but you can just as easily use any other document. The document has the following layout:				20200411 15:09:53
