helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>HTML WebQuery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; inserting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external data; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>web pages; importing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebQuery filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources; external data\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"webquery\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/webquery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\"\>Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	ca-XR	With the help of the \<emph\>Web Page Query ($[officename] Calc)\</emph\> import filter, you can insert tables from HTML documents in a Calc spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	ca-XR	You can use the same method to insert ranges defined by name from a Calc or Microsoft Excel spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ca-XR	The following insert methods are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	ca-XR	Inserting by Dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	ca-XR	Set the cell cursor at the cell where the new content will be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Link to External Data\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\"\>External Data\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	ca-XR	Enter the URL of the HTML document or the name of the spreadsheet. Press Enter when finished. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open a file selection dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	ca-XR	In the large list box of the dialog, select the named ranges or tables you want to insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	ca-XR	You can also specify that the ranges or tables are updated every n seconds.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	ca-XR	The import filter can create names for cell ranges on the fly. As much formatting as possible is retained, while the filter intentionally does not load any images.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149021				0	ca-XR	Inserting by Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	ca-XR	Open two documents: the $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in which the external data is to be inserted (target document) and the document from which the external data derives (source document).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	ca-XR	In the target document open the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	ca-XR	In the lower combo box of the Navigator select the source document. The Navigator now shows the range names and database ranges or the tables contained in the source document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842	20			0	ca-XR	In the Navigator select the \<emph\>Insert as link\</emph\> drag mode \<image id=\"img_id3152985\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	ca-XR	Drag the desired external data from the Navigator into the target document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	ca-XR	If you have loaded an HTML document with the \<emph\>Web Page Query\</emph\> filter as the source document, you will find the tables in the Navigator, named continuously from "HTML_table1" onwards, and also two range names that have been created:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152873				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_all\</item\> - designates the entire document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149897				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_tables\</item\> - designates all HTML tables in the document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149126				0	ca-XR	Editing the external data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3159228				0	ca-XR	Open \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>. Here you can edit the link to the external data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154650				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External data dialog\"\>External data dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				20200411 15:09:53
