helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	ca-XR	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	ca-XR	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	ca-XR	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	ca-XR	The \<emph\>Import dBASE files\</emph\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	ca-XR	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	ca-XR	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	ca-XR	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	ca-XR	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialog, select "dBASE".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	ca-XR	Locate the directory that contains the dBASE file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	ca-XR	To Save a Spreadsheet as a dBASE File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBASE file".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBASE file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
