helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1495406				0	ca-XR	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed, except the diagonal lines, which will be removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9269386				0	ca-XR	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3593554				0	ca-XR	User Defined Settings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4018066				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8004699				0	ca-XR	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8037659				0	ca-XR	Line types				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2305978				0	ca-XR	Image				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8716086				0	ca-XR	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3978087				0	ca-XR	A black line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4065065				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id9379863\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9379863\"\>solid line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6987823				0	ca-XR	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1209143				0	ca-XR	A gray line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6653340				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id6972563\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_gray.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6972563\"\>gray line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2278817				0	ca-XR	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5374919				0	ca-XR	A white line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id52491				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3801080\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_white.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3801080\"\>white line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id372325				0	ca-XR	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7282937				0	ca-XR	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4230780				0	ca-XR	Select a single cell, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1712393				0	ca-XR	Click the lower edge to set a very thin line as a lower border. All other lines will be removed from the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5149693				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id9467452\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_6.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9467452\"\>setting a thin lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5759453				0	ca-XR	Choose a thicker line style and click the lower edge. This sets a thicker line as a lower border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6342051				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id7431562\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7431562\"\>setting a thick line as a border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5775322				0	ca-XR	Click the second \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icon from the left to set all four borders. Then repeatedly click the lower edge until a white line is shown. This removes the lower border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2882778				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id8155766.00000001\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_8.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8155766.00000001\"\>removing lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8102053				0	ca-XR	You can combine several line types and styles. The last image shows how to set thick outer borders (the thick black lines), while any diagonal lines inside the cell will not be touched (gray lines).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2102420				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id5380718\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_9.png\" width=\"1.2602in\" height=\"1.1252in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5380718\"\>advanced example for cell borders\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Validity of Cell Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156442				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>values; limiting on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>limits; specifying value limits on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>permitted cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error messages; defining for incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>actions in case of incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips; defining text for cell input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments;help text for cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining input help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>macros; running when incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; validity check\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"validity\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/validity.xhp\" name=\"Validity of Cell Contents\"\>Validity of Cell Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	ca-XR	For each cell, you can define entries to be valid. Invalid entries to a cell will be rejected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	ca-XR	The validity rule is activated when a new value is entered. If an invalid value has already been inserted into the cell, or if you insert a value in the cell either with drag-and-drop or by copying and pasting, the validity rule will not take effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id5174718				0	ca-XR	You can choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective\</emph\> at any time and choose the command \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>\<emph\>Mark Invalid Data\</emph\>\</link\> to display which cells contain invalid values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603				0	ca-XR	Using Cell Contents Validity				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	ca-XR	Select the cells for which you want to define a new validity rule.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837	8			0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Validity\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156020	9			0	ca-XR	On the \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> tab page, enter the conditions for new values entered into cells. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159208				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Allow\</emph\> field, select an option.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011				0	ca-XR	If you select "Whole Numbers", values such as "12.5" are not allowed. Choosing "Date" allows date information both in the local date format as well as in the form of a \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"serial date\"\>serial date\</link\>. Similarly, the "Time" condition permits time values such as "12:00" or serial time numbers. "Text Length" stipulates that cells are allowed to contain text only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id9224829				0	ca-XR	Select "List" to enter a list of valid entries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149317				0	ca-XR	Select the next condition under \<emph\>Data\</emph\>. According to what you choose, additional options will be selectable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	ca-XR	After you have determined the conditions for cell validity, you can use the other two tab pages to create message boxes:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159261				0	ca-XR	On the \<emph\>Input Help\</emph\> tab page, enter the title and the text of the tip, which will then be displayed if the cell is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396				0	ca-XR	On the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page, select the action to be carried out in the event of an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3147416				0	ca-XR	If you select "Stop" as the action, invalid entries are not accepted, and the previous cell contents are retained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033				0	ca-XR	Select "Warning" or "Information" to display a dialog in which the entry can either be canceled or accepted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	ca-XR	If you select "Macro", then by using the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button you can specify a macro to be run in the event of an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149011	35			0	ca-XR	To display the error message, select \<emph\>Show error message when invalid values are entered\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	ca-XR	After changing the action for a cell on the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page and closing the dialog with OK, you must first select another cell before the change takes effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3154805				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Validity\"\>Data - Validity\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	ca-XR	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	ca-XR	The Find & Replace dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	ca-XR	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	ca-XR	To find formulas or values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	ca-XR	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	ca-XR	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	ca-XR	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	ca-XR	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	ca-XR	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	ca-XR	Finding text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	ca-XR	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	ca-XR	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	ca-XR	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	ca-XR	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	ca-XR	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	ca-XR	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	ca-XR	The Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	ca-XR	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	ca-XR	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheets on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repeating;columns/rows on printed pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; printing on all sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; rows/columns as table headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings;repeating rows/columns as\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153727				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"print_title_row\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_title_row.xhp\" name=\"Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\"\>Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	ca-XR	If you have a sheet that is so large that it will be printed multiple pages, you can set up rows or columns to repeat on each printed page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	ca-XR	As an example, If you want to print the top two rows of the sheet as well as the first column (A)on all pages, do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Edit\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Edit Print Ranges\</emph\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	ca-XR	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	ca-XR	The dialog shrinks so that you can see more of the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	ca-XR	Select the first two rows and, for this example, click cell A1 and drag to A2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	ca-XR	In the shrunk dialog you will see $1:$2. Rows 1 and 2 are now rows to repeat.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	ca-XR	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area. The dialog is restored again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	ca-XR	If you also want column A as a column to repeat, click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	ca-XR	Click column A (not in the column header).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	ca-XR	Click the icon again at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	ca-XR	Rows to repeat are rows from the sheet. You can define headers and footers to be printed on each print page independently of this in \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155380				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146113				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\"\>Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
