helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154686				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; referencing cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; referencing by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references;inserting by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;references, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154686				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"cellreference_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreference_dragdrop.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\"\>Referencing Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	ca-XR	With the help of the Navigator you can reference cells from one sheet to another sheet in the same document or in a different document. The cells can be inserted as a copy, link, or hyperlink. The range to be inserted must be defined with a name in the original file so that it can be inserted in the target file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	ca-XR	Open the document that contains the source cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	ca-XR	To set the source range as the range, select the cells and choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. Save the source document, and do not close it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	ca-XR	Open the sheet in which you want to insert something.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154732				0	ca-XR	Open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>. In the lower box of the Navigator select the source file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	ca-XR	In the Navigator, the source file object appears under "Range names".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	ca-XR	Using the \<emph\>Drag Mode\</emph\> icon in Navigator, choose whether you want the reference to be a hyperlink, link, or copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	ca-XR	Click the name under "Range names" in the Navigator, and drag into the cell of the current sheet where you want to insert the reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreference_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	ca-XR	This method can also be used to insert a range from another sheet of the same document into the current sheet. Select the active document as source in step 4 above.				20200411 15:09:53
