helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-defined Number Formats\"\>User-defined Number Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	ca-XR	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	ca-XR	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	ca-XR	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				20200411 15:09:53
