helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150691				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3147535				0	ca-XR	DEC2HEX(Number; Places)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3152820				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is a decimal number. If Number is negative, the function returns a hexadecimal number with 10 characters (40 bits). The most significant bit is the sign bit, the other 39 bits return the value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Places\</emph\> means the number of places to be output.				20200411 15:09:53
