helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is a decimal number. If Number is negative, the function returns an octal number with 10 characters (30 bits). The most significant bit is the sign bit, the other 29 bits return the value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	par_id3152587				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Places\</emph\> means the number of places to be output.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060115.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147482				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
