helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156396	31			0	ca-XR	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019	32			0	ca-XR	Following you will find a description of those functions, which are called at the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>external DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150038	33			0	ca-XR	For all \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> functions, the following applies:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3157876				0	ca-XR	void CALLTYPE fn(out, in1, in2, ...)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147616				0	ca-XR	Output: Resulting value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159119				0	ca-XR	Input: Any number of types (double&, char*, double*, char**, Cell area), where the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Cell area\"\>Cell area\</link\> is an array of types double array, string array, or cell array.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653				0	ca-XR	GetFunctionCount()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3152981				0	ca-XR	Returns the number of functions without the management functions of the reference parameter. Each function has a unique number between 0 and nCount-1. This number will be needed for the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionData\"\>GetFunctionData\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetParameterDescription\"\>GetParameterDescription\</link\> functions later.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	ca-XR	void CALLTYPE GetFunctionCount(USHORT& nCount)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154677				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146940				0	ca-XR	USHORT &nCount:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	ca-XR	Output: Reference to a variable, which is supposed to contain the number of Add-In functions. For example: If the Add-In provides 5 functions for $[officename] Calc, then nCount=5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147476				0	ca-XR	GetFunctionData()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154841				0	ca-XR	Determines all the important information about an Add-In function.				20200411 15:09:53
