helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145388				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>FINV function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>inverse F probability distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145388				0	ca-XR	FINV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3155089				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_FINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the F probability distribution.\</ahelp\> The F distribution is used for F tests in order to set the relation between two differing data sets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153816				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	ca-XR	FINV(Number; DegreesFreedom1; DegreesFreedom2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3146866	6			0	ca-XR	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is probability value for which the inverse F distribution is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914	7			0	ca-XR	            \<emph\>DegreesFreedom1\</emph\> is the number of degrees of freedom in the numerator of the F distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3148607	8			0	ca-XR	            \<emph\>DegreesFreedom2\</emph\> is the number of degrees of freedom in the denominator of the F distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156021				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3145073	10			0	ca-XR	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=FINV(0.5;5;10)\</item\> yields 0.93.				20200411 15:09:53
