helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903205379				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Returns the Gamma function value.\</ahelp\> Note that GAMMAINV is not the inverse of GAMMA, but of GAMMADIST.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id0119200903271613				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903271614				0	ca-XR	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number for which the Gamma function value is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154841				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>GAMMAINV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154841				0	ca-XR	GAMMAINV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060182.xhp	0	help	par_id3153932				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_GAMMAINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the Gamma cumulative distribution GAMMADIST.\</ahelp\> This function allows you to search for variables with different distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
