helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Statistical Functions Part Four				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"mq\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060184.xhp\" name=\"Statistical Functions Part Four\"\>Statistical Functions Part Four\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154511				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>MAX function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	ca-XR	MAX				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAX\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id9282509				0	ca-XR	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	ca-XR	MAX(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	6			0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166426				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>MAXA function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166426				0	ca-XR	MAXA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAXA\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments. In opposite to MAX, here you can enter text. The value of the text is 0.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id7689443				0	ca-XR	The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150516				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3166431				0	ca-XR	MAXA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Value1; Value2;...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156290				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156446				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200;"Text")\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149404				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAXA(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153820				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>MEDIAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153820				0	ca-XR	MEDIAN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MEDIAN\"\>Returns the median of a set of numbers. In a set containing an uneven number of values, the median will be the number in the middle of the set and in a set containing an even number of values, it will be the mean of the two values in the middle of the set.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148871				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	ca-XR	MEDIAN(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are values or ranges, which represent a sample. Each number can also be replaced by a reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144506				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	ca-XR	for an odd number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20;21)\</item\> returns 9 as the median value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	ca-XR	for an even number: \<item type=\"input\"\>=MEDIAN(1;5;9;20)\</item\> returns the average of the two middle values 5 and 9, thus 7.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154541				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>MIN function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154541				0	ca-XR	MIN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3143222				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MIN\"\>Returns the minimum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id2301400				0	ca-XR	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154651				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146964				0	ca-XR	MIN(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153486				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155523				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154734				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MIN(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the smallest value in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147504				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>MINA function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147504				0	ca-XR	MINA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147249				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MINA\"\>Returns the minimum value in a list of arguments. Here you can also enter text. The value of the text is 0.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id4294564				0	ca-XR	The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150435				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153336				0	ca-XR	MINA(Value1; Value2; ... Value30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146098				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Value1; Value2;...Value30\</emph\> are values or ranges. Text has the value of 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148743				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147401				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINA(1;"Text";20)\</item\> returns 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MINA(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the smallest value in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166465				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>AVEDEV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages;statistical functions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
