helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K1				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTB\"\>Average the values of cells in a range that meet a criteria.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K1				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K1				0	ca-XR	AVERAGEIF( Reference R ; Criterion C [ ; Reference A ] )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K1				0	ca-XR	 If reference A is omitted, averages the values of cells in the reference range R that meet the Criterion C. If reference A is given, averages the values of cells of a range that is constructed using the top left cell of reference A and applying the dimensions, shape and size, of reference R.  Does not accept constant values as reference parameters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K1				0	ca-XR	If no cell in range R matches the Criterion C, an Error is returned. If no Numbers are in the range to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K1				0	ca-XR	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K1				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIF(A1:A50;">"0)\</item\>will return the average of A1:A50 of all positive values in the range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148754K2				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>AVERAGEIFS function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754K2				0	ca-XR	AVERAGEIFS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K2				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTC\"\>Average the values of cells that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K2				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K2				0	ca-XR	AVERAGEIFS( Reference A ; Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K2				0	ca-XR	Averages the values of cells in the reference range A that meet the Criterion C1 in the reference range R1 and the Criterion C2 in the reference range R2, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K2				0	ca-XR	All reference ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned. A logical AND is applied between each array result of each selection; a cell of reference range A is evaluated only if the same position in each array is the result of a Criterion match. If no numbers are in the result set to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K2				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K2				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIFS(A1:A50;B1:B25;">"0)\</item\>+will return the average of A1:A50 if all cells in the range B1 to B25 are greater than 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153933				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>MODE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>most common value\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153933				0	ca-XR	MODE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MODALWERT\"\>Returns the most common value in a data set.\</ahelp\> If there are several values with the same frequency, it returns the smallest value. An error occurs when a value doesn't appear twice.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153003				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155950				0	ca-XR	MODE(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150337				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153571				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MODE(A1:A50)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149879				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>NEGBINOMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>negative binomial distribution\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149879				0	ca-XR	NEGBINOMDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155437				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NEGBINOMVERT\"\>Returns the negative binomial distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145351				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	ca-XR	NEGBINOMDIST(X; R; SP)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153044				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>X\</emph\> represents the value returned for unsuccessful tests.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151018				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>R\</emph\> represents the value returned for successful tests.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148878				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of the success of an attempt.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149539				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148770				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NEGBINOMDIST(1;1;0.5)\</item\> returns 0.25.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155516				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>NORMINV function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>normal distribution;inverse of\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155516				0	ca-XR	NORMINV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154634				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NORMINV\"\>Returns the inverse of the normal cumulative distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153227				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147534				0	ca-XR	NORMINV(Number; Mean; StDev)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154950				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> represents the probability value used to determine the inverse normal distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150690				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> represents the mean value in the normal distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148594				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> represents the standard deviation of the normal distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155822				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMINV(0.9;63;5)\</item\> returns 69.41. If the average egg weighs 63 grams with a standard deviation of 5, then there will be 90% probability that the egg will not be heavier than 69.41g grams.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153722				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>NORMDIST function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>density function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153722				0	ca-XR	NORMDIST				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NORMVERT\"\>Returns the density function or the normal cumulative distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083282				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150613				0	ca-XR	NORMDIST(Number; Mean; StDev; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value of the distribution based on which the normal distribution is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146063				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> is the mean value of the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156295				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>StDev\</emph\> is the standard deviation of the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>C\</emph\> is optional. \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calculates the density function, \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calculates the distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152972				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMDIST(70;63;5;0)\</item\> returns 0.03.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149448				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMDIST(70;63;5;1)\</item\> returns 0.92.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152934				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>PEARSON function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152934				0	ca-XR	PEARSON				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153216				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PEARSON\"\>Returns the Pearson product moment correlation coefficient r.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147081				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156133				0	ca-XR	PEARSON(Data1; Data2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151272				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Data1\</emph\> represents the array of the first data set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153279				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Data2\</emph\> represents the array of the second data set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147567				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PEARSON(A1:A30;B1:B30)\</item\> returns the Pearson correlation coefficient of both data sets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152806				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>PHI function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152806				0	ca-XR	PHI				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PHI\"\>Returns the values of the distribution function for a standard normal distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154748				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149976				0	ca-XR	PHI(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> represents the value based on which the standard normal distribution is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153621				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155849				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PHI(2.25) \</item\>= 0.03				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3143236				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PHI(-2.25)\</item\> = 0.03				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149286				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PHI(0)\</item\> = 0.4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153985				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>POISSON function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153985				0	ca-XR	POISSON				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154298				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POISSON\"\>Returns the Poisson distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159183				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146093				0	ca-XR	POISSON(Number; Mean; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147253				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> represents the value based on which the Poisson distribution is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Mean\</emph\> represents the middle value of the Poisson distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149200				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>C\</emph\> (optional) = 0 or False calculates the density function; \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 or True calculates the distribution. When omitted, the default value True is inserted when you save the document, for best compatibility with other programs and older versions of %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159347				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150113				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=POISSON(60;50;1)\</item\> returns 0.93.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153100				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>PERCENTILE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153100				0	ca-XR	PERCENTILE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154940				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUANTIL\"\>Returns the alpha-percentile of data values in an array.\</ahelp\> A percentile returns the scale value for a data series which goes from the smallest (Alpha=0) to the largest value (alpha=1) of a data series. For \<item type=\"literal\"\>Alpha\</item\> = 25%, the percentile means the first quartile; \<item type=\"literal\"\>Alpha\</item\> = 50% is the MEDIAN.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150531				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	ca-XR	PERCENTILE(Data; Alpha)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153054				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> represents the array of data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154212				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Alpha\</emph\> represents the percentage of the scale between 0 and 1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154290				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PERCENTILE(A1:A50;0.1)\</item\> represents the value in the data set, which equals 10% of the total data scale in A1:A50.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148807				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>PERCENTRANK function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148807				0	ca-XR	PERCENTRANK				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUANTILSRANG\"\>Returns the percentage rank of a value in a sample.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147512				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147238				0	ca-XR	PERCENTRANK(Data; Value)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154266				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> represents the array of data in the sample.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148475				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Value\</emph\> represents the value whose percentile rank must be determined.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149163				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PERCENTRANK(A1:A50;50)\</item\> returns the percentage rank of the value 50 from the total range of all values found in A1:A50. If 50 falls outside the total range, an error message will appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166442				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>QUARTILE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166442				0	ca-XR	QUARTILE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146958				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUARTILE\"\>Returns the quartile of a data set.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152942				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153684				0	ca-XR	QUARTILE(Data; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Data\</emph\> represents the array of data in the sample.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155589				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> represents the type of quartile. (0 = MIN, 1 = 25%, 2 = 50% (MEDIAN), 3 = 75% and 4 = MAX.)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149103				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3159276				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=QUARTILE(A1:A50;2)\</item\> returns the value of which 50% of the scale corresponds to the lowest to highest values in the range A1:A50.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159399				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>automatic hyphenation in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation; in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>syllables in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	ca-XR	Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068	2			0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"silben\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Hyphenate\"\>The \<emph\>Hyphenation \</emph\>command calls the dialog for setting the hyphenation in $[officename] Calc.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	ca-XR	You can only turn on the automatic hyphenation in $[officename] Calc when the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05340300.xhp\" name=\"row break\"\>row break\</link\> feature is active.				20200411 15:09:53
