helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153200				0	ca-XR	COUPNUM(Settlement; Maturity; Frequency; Basis)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159406				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154720				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Frequency\</emph\> is the number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149319				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460				0	ca-XR	A security is purchased on 2001-01-25; the date of maturity is 2001-11-15. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how many interest dates are there?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640				0	ca-XR	=COUPNUM("2001-01-25"; "2001-11-15"; 2; 3) returns 2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149339				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>IPMT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>periodic amortizement rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149339				0	ca-XR	IPMT				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154522				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZINSZ\"\>Calculates the periodic amortizement for an investment with regular payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153266				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151283				0	ca-XR	IPMT(Rate; Period; NPer; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147313				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145158				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Period\</emph\> is the period, for which the compound interest is calculated. Period=NPER if compound interest for the last period is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147577				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods, during which annuity is paid.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156211				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present cash value in sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151213				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired value (future value) at the end of the periods.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154195				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> is the due date for the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150102				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149438				0	ca-XR	What is the interest rate during the fifth period (year) if the constant interest rate is 5% and the cash value is 15,000 currency units? The periodic payment is seven years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150496				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=IPMT(5%;5;7;15000)\</item\> = -352.97 currency units. The compound interest during the fifth period (year) is 352.97 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151205				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;future values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;constant interest rates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>FV function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151205				0	ca-XR	FV				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZW\"\>Returns the future value of an investment based on periodic, constant payments and a constant interest rate (Future Value).\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155178				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145215				0	ca-XR	FV(Rate; NPer; Pmt; PV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156029				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>NPer\</emph\> is the total number of periods (payment period).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the annuity paid regularly per period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> (optional) is the (present) cash value of an investment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150999				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) defines whether the payment is due at the beginning or the end of a period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN114D8				0	ca-XR	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146800				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146813				0	ca-XR	What is the value at the end of an investment if the interest rate is 4% and the payment period is two years, with a periodic payment of 750 currency units. The investment has a present value of 2,500 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149302				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FV(4%;2;750;2500) \</item\>= -4234.00 currency units. The value at the end of the investment is 4234.00 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155912				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>FVSCHEDULE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>future values;varying interest rates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155912				0	ca-XR	FVSCHEDULE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3163726				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_FVSCHEDULE\"\>Calculates the accumulated value of the starting capital for a series of periodically varying interest rates.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149571				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148891				0	ca-XR	FVSCHEDULE(Principal; Schedule)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148904				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Principal\</emph\> is the starting capital.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148562				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Schedule\</emph\> is a series of interest rates, for example, as a range H3:H5 or as a (List) (see example).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147288				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148638				0	ca-XR	1000 currency units have been invested in for three years. The interest rates were 3%, 4% and 5% per annum. What is the value after three years?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3156358				0	ca-XR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FVSCHEDULE(1000;{0.03;0.04;0.05})\</item\> returns 1124.76.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156435				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;number of payment periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>payment periods;number of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of payment periods\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>NPER function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156435				0	ca-XR	NPER				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZZR\"\>Returns the number of periods for an investment based on periodic, constant payments and a constant interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147216				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155934				0	ca-XR	NPER(Rate; Pmt; PV; FV; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Rate\</emph\> is the periodic interest rate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149042				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Pmt\</emph\> is the constant annuity paid in each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153134				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value (cash value) in a sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the future value, which is reached at the end of the last period.				20200411 15:09:53
