helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id1939451				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to shrink or restore the dialog. You can click or select cells in the sheet. You can enter a cell reference manually in the input box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to remove the row from the list. Any rows from below this row move up.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Options dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to solve the equation with the current settings. The dialog settings are retained until you close the current document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5474410				0	ca-XR	To solve equations with the solver				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	ca-XR	The goal of the solver process is to find those variable values of an equation that result in an optimized value in the \<emph\>target cell\</emph\>, also named the "objective". You can choose whether the value in the target cell should be a maximum, a minimum, or approaching a given value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	ca-XR	The initial variable values are inserted in a rectangular cell range that you enter in the \<emph\>By changing cells\</emph\> box. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	ca-XR	You can define a series of limiting conditions that set constraints for some cells. For example, you can set the constraint that one of the variables or cells must not be bigger than another variable, or not bigger than a given value. You can also define the constraint that one or more variables must be integers (values without decimals), or binary values (where only 0 and 1 are allowed).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5323953				0	ca-XR	The default solver engine supports only linear equations.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Left				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02140400.xhp\" name=\"Left\"\>Left\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FillLeft\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Fills a selected range of at least two columns with the contents of the far right cell.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02140400.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	ca-XR	If a selected range has only one row, the content of the far right cell is copied into all other cells of the range. If several rows are selected, the far right cells are copied into the cells to the left.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Move or Copy a Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153360				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; moving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	ca-XR	Move or Copy a Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154686				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"tabelleverschiebenkopierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Move\"\>Moves or copies a sheet to a new location in the document or to a different document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id2282479				0	ca-XR	When you copy and paste cells containing \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060102.xhp\"\>date values\</link\> between different spreadsheets, both spreadsheet documents must be set to the same date base. If date bases differ, the displayed date values will change!				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163710				0	ca-XR	To Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:LB_DEST\"\>Indicates where the current sheet is to be moved or copied to.\</ahelp\> Select \<emph\>new document\</emph\> if you want to create a new location for the sheet to be moved or copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154012				0	ca-XR	Insert Before				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:LISTBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:LB_INSERT\"\>The current sheet is moved or copied in front of the selected sheet.\</ahelp\> The \<emph\>move to end position\</emph\> option places the current sheet at the end.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	ca-XR	Copy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\02180000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_MOVETAB:BTN_COPY\"\>Specifies that the sheet is to be copied. If the option is unmarked, the sheet is moved.\</ahelp\> Moving sheets is the default.				20200411 15:09:53
