helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156374				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150284				0	ca-XR	TBILLPRICE(Settlement; Maturity; Discount)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154059				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Settlement\</emph\> is the date of purchase of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154073				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Maturity\</emph\> is the date on which the security matures (expires).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Discount\</emph\> is the percentage discount upon acquisition of the security.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153373				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155542				0	ca-XR	Settlement date: March 31 1999, maturity date: June 1 1999, discount: 9 per cent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154578				0	ca-XR	The price of the treasury bill is worked out as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154592				0	ca-XR	=TBILLPRICE("1999-03-31";"1999-06-01"; 0.09) returns 98.45.				20200411 15:09:53
