helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030700.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145119				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030700.xhp\" name=\"Fill Mode\"\>Fill Mode\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151246				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AuditingFillMode\"\>Activates the Fill Mode in the Detective. The mouse pointer changes to a special symbol, and you can click any cell to see a trace to the precedent cell.\</ahelp\> To exit this mode, press Escape or click the \<emph\>End Fill Mode\</emph\> command in the context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	ca-XR	The \<emph\>Fill Mode\</emph\> function is identical to the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030100.xhp\" name=\"Trace Precedent\"\>Trace Precedent\</link\> command if you call this mode for the first time. Use the context menu to select further options for the Fill Mode and to exit this mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	DAYS360 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148555				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>DAYS360 function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148555				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"days360\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_days360.xhp\"\>DAYS360\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156032				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAGE360\"\>Returns the difference between two dates based on the 360 day year used in interest calculations.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155347				0	ca-XR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3155313				0	ca-XR	DAYS360("Date1"; "Date2"; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	ca-XR	If \<emph\>Date2\</emph\> is earlier than \<emph\>Date1\</emph\>, the function will return a negative number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3151064				0	ca-XR	The optional argument \<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of difference calculation. If Type = 0 or if the argument is missing, the US method (NASD, National Association of Securities Dealers) is used. If Type <> 0, the European method is used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148641				0	ca-XR	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_days360.xhp	0	help	par_id3156348				0	ca-XR	=DAYS360("2000-01-01";NOW()) returns the number of interest days from January 1, 2000 until today.				20200411 15:09:53
