helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>From File\</emph\>, locate the file containing the styles that you want to use, and then click name, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Using Wildcards in Text Searches				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150099				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>wildcards, see regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>searching; with wildcards\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>regular expressions;searching\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>examples for regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters;finding all\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>invisible characters;finding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;searching\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150099				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"search_regexp\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/search_regexp.xhp\"\>Using Wildcards in Text Searches\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345516				0	ca-XR	Wildcards or placeholders can be used to search for some unspecified or even invisible characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	ca-XR	You can use wildcards when you find and replace text in a document. For example, "s.n" finds "sun" and "son".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Find & Replace\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id2142399				0	ca-XR	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More Options\</item\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	ca-XR	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Regular expressions\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	ca-XR	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	ca-XR	Regular Expression Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	ca-XR	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	ca-XR	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	ca-XR	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	ca-XR	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345545				0	ca-XR	The wildcard for a tab character is \\t.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	ca-XR	A search using a regular expression will work only within one paragraph. To search using a regular expression in more than one paragraph, do a separate search in each paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Wildcards\"\>List of Wildcards\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
