helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"sections\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/sections.xhp\" name=\"Using Sections\"\>Using Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	ca-XR	Sections are named blocks of text, including graphics or objects, that you can use in a number of ways:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149284				0	ca-XR	To prevent text from being edited.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	ca-XR	To show or hide text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149647				0	ca-XR	To reuse text and graphics from other $[officename] documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	ca-XR	To insert sections of text that uses a different column layout than the current page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855				0	ca-XR	A section contains at least one paragraph. When you select a text and create a section, a paragraph break is automatically inserted at the end of the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	ca-XR	You can insert sections from a text document, or an entire text document as a section into another text document. You can also insert sections from a text document as links in another text document, or in the same document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367	39			0	ca-XR	To insert a new paragraph immediately before or after a section, click in front or behind the section, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	ca-XR	Sections and Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	ca-XR	You can insert sections into an existing section. For example, you can insert a section containing two columns into a section that contains one column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154845				0	ca-XR	A section layout, for example on the number of columns, has priority over the page layout defined in a page style.				20200411 15:09:53
