helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154243				0	ca-XR	To Enable Automatic Numbering and Bulleting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152830	29			0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab, and then select “Apply numbering – symbol”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152867				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect\</emph\>, and ensure that \<emph\>While Typing\</emph\> is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id2357860				0	ca-XR	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152897				0	ca-XR	To Create a Numbered or Bulleted List While You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	ca-XR	Type 1., i., or I. to start a numbered list. Type * or - to start a bulleted list. You can also type a right parenthesis after the number instead of a period , for example, 1) or i).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147794				0	ca-XR	Enter a space, type your text, and then press Enter. The new paragraph automatically receives the next number or bullet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147814				0	ca-XR	Press Enter again to finish the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	ca-XR	You can start a numbered list with any number.				20200411 15:09:53
