helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>references; inserting cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting and updating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"references\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Cross-References\"\>Inserting Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	ca-XR	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	ca-XR	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	ca-XR	Cross-Referencing Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	ca-XR	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	ca-XR	To Insert a Target				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	ca-XR	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list, select “Set Reference”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	ca-XR	Type a name for the target in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box. The selected text is displayed in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	ca-XR	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>. The name of the target is added to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Selection\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	ca-XR	Leave the dialog open and proceed to the next section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153370				0	ca-XR	To Create a Cross-Reference to a Target				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7032074				0	ca-XR	Position the cursor in the text where you want to insert a cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7796868				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\> to open the dialog, if it is not open already.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149980				0	ca-XR	Cross-Referencing an Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	ca-XR	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	ca-XR	Click in the document where you want to insert the cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3151092				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151115				0	ca-XR	Updating Cross-References				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	ca-XR	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7321390				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>View - Fields\</emph\> to switch between viewing the reference names and the reference contents.				20200411 15:09:53
