helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"dragdroptext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/dragdroptext.xhp\" name=\"Moving and Copying Text in Documents\"\>Moving and Copying Text in Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	ca-XR	Select the text that you want to move or copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155606				0	ca-XR	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154236				0	ca-XR	To move the selected text, drag the text to a different location in the document and release. While you drag, the mouse pointer changes to include a gray box.\<br/\>\<image id=\"img_id3153148\" src=\"res/helpimg/movedata.png\" width=\"0.3335in\" height=\"0.3335in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153148\"\>Mouse cursor moving data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257	14			0	ca-XR	To copy the selected text, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you drag. The mouse pointer changes to include a plus sign (+).\<br/\>\<image id=\"img_id3152868\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"0.3335in\" height=\"0.3335in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152868\"\>Mouse cursor copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Hiding Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>text; hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables;for hiding text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856	1			0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"hidden_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	ca-XR	You can use fields and sections to hide or display text in your document if a condition is met.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	ca-XR	Before you can hide text, you must first create a variable to use in the condition for hiding the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id5174108				0	ca-XR	To Create a Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153131				0	ca-XR	Click in your document and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640	21			0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab and click "Set Variable" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970	22			0	ca-XR	Click "General" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	ca-XR	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149869				0	ca-XR	Enter a value for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	ca-XR	To hide the variable in your document, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	ca-XR	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156245				0	ca-XR	To Hide Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145391				0	ca-XR	Click in the document where you want to add the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409	5			0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	29			0	ca-XR	Click "Hidden Text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154404				0	ca-XR	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371	31			0	ca-XR	Type the text that you want to hide in the \<emph\>Hidden text \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	ca-XR	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	ca-XR	To Hide a Paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	ca-XR	Click in the paragraph where you want to add the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154872	35			0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	6			0	ca-XR	Click "Hidden Paragraph" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155947				0	ca-XR	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	ca-XR	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3793450				0	ca-XR	You must enable this feature by removing the check mark from menu \<emph\>View - Hidden Paragraphs\</emph\>. When the check mark is set, you cannot hide any paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
