helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155856				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>table mode selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>proportional distribution of tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative distribution of table cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; adapting the width by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard;modifying the behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>behavior of rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155856				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"tablemode\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/tablemode.xhp\" name=\"Modifying the Behavior of Rows and Columns for Table\"\>Modifying Rows and Columns by Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149835				0	ca-XR	When you insert or delete cells, rows or columns in a table, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options determine how the neighboring elements are affected. For example, you can only insert new rows and columns into a table with fixed row and column dimensions if space permits.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id7344279				0	ca-XR	Note that these properties are valid only for changes to the column width that are made using the keyboard. Using the mouse, you are free to make any column width changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3156110				0	ca-XR	To set the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Behavior of rows/columns\</item\> options for tables in text documents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</item\>, or use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed\</item\>, \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fixed/Proportional\</item\>, and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variable\</item\> icons on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table\</item\> Bar. There are three display modes for tables:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> - changes only affect the adjacent cell, and not the entire table. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cell becomes narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149613				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Fixed, proportional\</emph\> - changes affect the entire table, and wide cells shrink more than narrow cells. For example, when you widen a cell, the adjacent cells become proportionally narrower, but the width of the table remains constant.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\tablemode.xhp	0	help	par_id3149864				0	ca-XR	\<emph\>Variable\</emph\> - changes affect the table size. For example, when you widen a cell, the width of the table increases.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Using AutoText				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155521				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>AutoText\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>networks and AutoText directories\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blocks of text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155521				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"autotext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autotext.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoText\"\>Using AutoText\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	ca-XR	In $[officename] Writer, you can store text - also containing graphics, tables, and fields - as AutoText, so that you can quickly insert the text later on. If you want, you can also store formatted text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155539				0	ca-XR	To To Create an AutoText Entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	ca-XR	Select the text, text with graphics, table, or field that you want to save as an AutoText entry. A graphic can only be stored if it is anchored as a character and is preceded and followed by at least one text character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155581				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - AutoText\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147761				0	ca-XR	Select the category where you want to store the AutoText.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779				0	ca-XR	Type a name that is longer than four characters. This allows you to use the \<emph\>Display remainder of name as suggestion while typing\</emph\> AutoText option. If you want, you can modify the proposed shortcut.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147807	60			0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_idN10732				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147282				0	ca-XR	To Insert an AutoText Entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145597				0	ca-XR	Click in your document where you want to insert an AutoText entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615				0	ca-XR	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>\<emph\>Edit - AutoText\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145644				0	ca-XR	Select the AutoText that you want to insert, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668	30			0	ca-XR	You can also type the shortcut for an AutoText entry, and then press F3, or click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoText\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> bar, and then choose an AutoText entry. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155090	43			0	ca-XR	To quickly enter a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>fn\</item\>, and then press F3. If you insert more than one formula, the formulae are sequentially numbered. To insert dummy text, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>dt\</item\>, and then press F3. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155115				0	ca-XR	To Print a List of AutoText Entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155160				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> list, double-click "%PRODUCTNAME Macros - Gimmicks".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	ca-XR	Select "AutoText" and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>. A list of the current AutoText entries is generated in a separate text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151304				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151327				0	ca-XR	Using AutoText in Network Installations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151355				0	ca-XR	You can store AutoText entries in different directories on a network.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	ca-XR	For example, you can store "read-only" AutoText entries for your company on a central server, and user-defined AutoText entries in a local directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	ca-XR	The paths for the AutoText directories can be edited in the configuration.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154960				0	ca-XR	Two directories are listed here. The first entry is on the server installation and the second entry is in the user directory. If there are two AutoText entries with the same name in both directories, the entry from the user directory is used.				20200411 15:09:53
