helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2055421				0	ca-XR	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9836115				0	ca-XR	A black line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6485793				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id1237525\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1237525\"\>solid line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1454512				0	ca-XR	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4618671				0	ca-XR	A gray line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1239356				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id2688680\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_7.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2688680\"\>gray line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9474166				0	ca-XR	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1545457				0	ca-XR	A white line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1681875				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id7340617\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_8.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7340617\"\>white line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2316660				0	ca-XR	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5908688				0	ca-XR	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5118564				0	ca-XR	Select a single cell in a Writer table, then choose \<emph\>Table - Table properties - Borders\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id244758				0	ca-XR	Select a thick line style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7741325				0	ca-XR	To set a lower border, click the lower edge repeatedly until you see a thick line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id542313				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id4273506\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4273506\"\>setting thick lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2210760				0	ca-XR	All cells in a Writer table have at least a left and a lower line by default. Most cells on the table perimeter have more lines applied by default. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5400860				0	ca-XR	All lines that are shown in white in the preview will be removed from the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Using Smart Tags				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155622				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>options;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>disabling;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;smart tags\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3563951				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"smarttags\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/smarttags.xhp\"\>Using Smart Tags\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id368358				0	ca-XR	Smart Tags provide additional information and functionality to specified words in a Writer document. The available features can be different for different Smart Tags extensions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id9298379				0	ca-XR	Installing Smart Tags				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	ca-XR	Smart Tags can be supplied as \<link href=\"text/shared/01/packagemanager.xhp\"\>extensions\</link\> to %PRODUCTNAME Writer. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	ca-XR	To install a Smart Tag, do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id3856013				0	ca-XR	Save the *.oxt extension file to your harddrive, then double-click the *.oxt file in your file manager. Alternatively, in %PRODUCTNAME choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> to open the Extension Manager, click Add and browse to the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id7814264				0	ca-XR	Click a Smart Tag *.oxt file link on a web page and open the link with the default application. This requires a properly configured Web browser.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id8142338				0	ca-XR	Smart Tags Menu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1917477				0	ca-XR	Any text in a Writer document can be marked with a Smart Tag, by default a magenta colored underline. You can change the color in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Appearance\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id192266				0	ca-XR	When you point to a Smart Tag, a tip help informs you to Ctrl-click to open the Smart Tags menu. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the marked text and open the context menu by Shift+F10.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1998962				0	ca-XR	In the Smart Tags menu you see the available actions that are defined for this Smart Tag. Choose an option from the menu. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Smart Tags Options\</item\> command opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page of Tools - Autocorrect Options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	hd_id2376476				0	ca-XR	To Enable and Disable Smart Tags				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id349131				0	ca-XR	When you have installed at least one Smart Tags extension, you see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040700.xhp\"\>Smart Tags\</link\> page in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Autocorrect Options\</item\>. Use this dialog to enable or disable Smart Tags and to manage the installed tags.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\smarttags.xhp	0	help	par_id1216467				0	ca-XR	Text that is recognized as a Smart Tag is not checked by the automatic spellcheck.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155186				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing or deleting entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing or deleting entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;entries of indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;table/index entries\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155186				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"indices_delete\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_delete.xhp\" name=\"Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries\"\>Editing or Deleting Index and Table Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	12			0	ca-XR	Index entries are inserted as fields into your document. To view fields in your document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View\</item\> and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Field Shadings\</item\> is selected. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155507				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor immediately in front of the index entry in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155526	16			0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Index Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3154238				0	ca-XR	To change the entry, enter different text in the \<emph\>Entry\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	ca-XR	To remove the entry, click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_delete.xhp	0	help	par_id3155893				0	ca-XR	To cycle through the index entries in your document, click the next or the previous arrows in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02160000.xhp\" name=\"Edit Index Entry dialog\"\>\<emph\>Edit Index Entry\</emph\> dialog\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Printing a Brochure				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	bm_id6743064				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>printing; individual brochures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>booklet printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brochures; printing individual\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F6				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"print_brochure\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_brochure.xhp\"\>Printing a Brochure\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	ca-XR	You can print a Writer document as a brochure or a booklet. That is, Writer prints two pages on each side of the paper, so that when you fold the paper, you can read the document as a book.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DE				0	ca-XR	When you create a document that you want to print as a brochure, use portrait orientation for the pages. Writer applies the brochure layout when you print the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	ca-XR	To Print a Brochure				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B6				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	ca-XR	In the properties dialog for your printer, set the paper orientation to landscape.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_id8947416				0	ca-XR	If your printer prints duplex, and because brochures always print in landscape mode, you should use the "duplex - short edge" setting in your printer setup dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10628				0	ca-XR	Return to \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, and click the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1062C				0	ca-XR	Select \<emph\>Brochure\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10740				0	ca-XR	For a printer that automatically prints on both sides of a page, specify to include "All pages".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	ca-XR	If %PRODUCTNAME prints the pages in the wrong order, open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, select \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>, and then print the document again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Finding and Replacing in Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id1163670				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>finding; text/text formats/styles/objects\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>replacing; text and text formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>styles;finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>text formats; finding\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>formats; finding and replacing\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>searching; formats\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>objects;finding by Navigator\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>Asian languages;search options\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8568681				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Writer\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id611285				0	ca-XR	In text documents you can find words, formatting, styles, and more. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all results at once, then apply another format or replace the words by other text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id6226081				0	ca-XR	The Find & Replace dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6702780				0	ca-XR	To find text within the whole document, open the Find & Replace dialog without any active text selection. If you want to search only a part of your document, first select that part of text, then open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158970				0	ca-XR	To Find Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6957304				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2164677				0	ca-XR	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5684072				0	ca-XR	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4377269				0	ca-XR	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Writer will show you the next text that is equal to your entry. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found text. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1371807				0	ca-XR	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next text without opening the dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id924100				0	ca-XR	Alternatively, you can use the icons at the lower right of the document to navigate to the next text or to any other object in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9359416				0	ca-XR	When you click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>, Writer selects all text that is equal to your entry. Now you can for example set all found text to bold, or apply a character style to all at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id5891598				0	ca-XR	To Replace Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1780755				0	ca-XR	Unlike searching text, replacing text cannot be restricted to the current selection only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2467421				0	ca-XR	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4286935				0	ca-XR	Enter the text to search in the \<emph\>Search for \</emph\>text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9959410				0	ca-XR	Enter the text to replace the found text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id24109				0	ca-XR	Either click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> or \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id703451				0	ca-XR	When you click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>, Writer will search the whole document for the text in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, starting at the current cursor position. When text is found, Writer highlights the text and waits for your response. Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> to replace the highlighted text in the document with the text in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box. Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> to advance to the next found text without replacing the current selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7540818				0	ca-XR	When you click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>, Writer replaces all text that matches your entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id9908444				0	ca-XR	To Find Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8413953				0	ca-XR	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain Paragraph Style is assigned, for example the "Heading 2" style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2696920				0	ca-XR	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id896938				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9147007				0	ca-XR	Check \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for Styles\</item\>.\<br/\>The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> text box now is a list box, where you can select any of the Paragraph Styles that are applied in the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id679342				0	ca-XR	Select the style to search for, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3231299				0	ca-XR	To Find Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8087405				0	ca-XR	You want to find all text in your document to which a certain direct character formatting is assigned. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3406170				0	ca-XR	Finding formats only finds direct character attributes, it does not find attributes applied as part of a style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2448805				0	ca-XR	Choose Edit - Find & Replace to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4542985				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4679403				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7783745				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id5597094				0	ca-XR	More options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9919431				0	ca-XR	The similarity search can find text that is almost the same as your search text. You can set the number of characters that are allowed to differ.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id8533280				0	ca-XR	Check the \<emph\>Similarity search\</emph\> option and optionally click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to change the settings. (Setting all three numbers to 1 works fine for English text.)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4646748				0	ca-XR	When you have enabled Asian language support under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>, the Find & Replace dialog offers options to search Asian text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2489394				0	ca-XR	The Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9934385				0	ca-XR	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects. You can also use the Navigator to move and arrange chapters, providing an outline view to your document. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4159062				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7421796				0	ca-XR	Use the Navigator for inserting objects, links and references within the same document or from other open documents. See the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/navigator.xhp\"\>Navigator\</link\> guide for more information.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6417432				0	ca-XR	Click the icon with the blue circle at the bottom right part of your document to open the small \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id4639728				0	ca-XR	Use the small Navigation window to quickly jump to the next object or find the next text in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Querying User Data in Fields or Conditions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153398				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>fields; user data\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>user data; querying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditions; user data fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, from specific users\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; hiding from specific users, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>user variables in conditions/fields\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
