helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147812				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Off AutoFormat and AutoCorrect\"\>Turning Off AutoCorrect\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833	2			0	ca-XR	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	ca-XR	To quickly undo an automatic correction or completion, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	ca-XR	To turn off most AutoCorrect features, remove the check mark from the menu \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - While Typing\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
