helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	ca-XR	You can select a table in a text document with a keyboard or with a mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	ca-XR	To select a table with the keyboard, move the cursor into the table, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all the cells are selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10633				0	ca-XR	To select a table with the mouse, move the mouse pointer to a position just above and left of the table. The mouse pointer becomes a diagonal arrow. Click to select the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	ca-XR	To select a row or column with the mouse, point to a position just left of the row or above the column. The mouse pointer becomes an arrow. Click to select the row or column.				20200411 15:09:53
