helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor in the index or table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155871				0	ca-XR	If you cannot place your cursor in the index or table of contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</item\>, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Enable\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Cursor in protected areas\</item\> section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	ca-XR	Right-click and choose an editing option from the menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	ca-XR	You can also make changes directly to an index or table of contents. Right-click in the index or table of contents, choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Protected from manual changes\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Inserting Sections				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>sections; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;inserting linked sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;linked sections, manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	ca-XR	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	ca-XR	To Insert a New Section				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	ca-XR	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103				0	ca-XR	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\> box, type a name for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	ca-XR	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635				0	ca-XR	To Insert a Section as a Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	ca-XR	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	ca-XR	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860				0	ca-XR	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browser, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104				0	ca-XR	Click in your document where you want to insert the linked section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\> box, type a name for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\> area, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\> check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>DDE\</item\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	ca-XR	Click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882				0	ca-XR	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149978				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Section\</item\> box, select the section that you want to insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Using the Direct Cursor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155178				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>text; cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text with direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>direct cursor; settings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>writing with direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cursor;direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>settings;direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155178				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"text_direct_cursor\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_direct_cursor.xhp\" name=\"Using the Direct Cursor\"\>Using the Direct Cursor\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3155908				0	ca-XR	The direct cursor allows you to enter text anywhere on a page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3155921				0	ca-XR	To set the behavior of the direct cursor, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	ca-XR	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools\</item\> bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Direct Cursor\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149846\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_shadowcursor.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149846\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	ca-XR	Click in a free space in the text document. The mouse pointer changes to reflect the alignment that will be applied to the text that you type:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C8				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id5471987\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircursleft.png\" width=\"0.1457in\" height=\"0.3228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5471987\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Align left				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E4				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id5730253\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircurscent.png\" width=\"0.2398in\" height=\"0.3228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5730253\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Centered				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id6953622\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircursright.png\" width=\"0.1563in\" height=\"0.3228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6953622\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Align right				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	ca-XR	Type your text. %PRODUCTNAME automatically inserts the required number of blank lines, and, if the options are enabled, tabs and spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation;manual/automatic\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>separation, see hyphenation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic hyphenation in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>manual hyphenation in text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"using_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Hyphenation\"\>Hyphenation\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918	31			0	ca-XR	By default, $[officename] moves words that do not fit on a line to the next line. If you want, you can use automatic or manual hyphenation to avoid this behavior: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155864				0	ca-XR	Automatic Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414				0	ca-XR	Automatic hyphenation inserts hyphens where they are needed in a paragraph. This option is only available for paragraph styles and individual paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	ca-XR	To Automatically Hyphenate Text in a Paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148850				0	ca-XR	Right-click in a paragraph, and choose \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	ca-XR	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3150101				0	ca-XR	In the Hyphenation area, select the Automatically check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153121				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149629				0	ca-XR	To Automatically Hyphenate Text in Multiple Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	ca-XR	If you want to automatically hyphenate more than one paragraph, use a paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	ca-XR	For example, enable the automatic hyphenation option for the "Default" paragraph style, and then apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149867				0	ca-XR	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to hyphenate, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3145106				0	ca-XR	Click the Text Flow tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Hyphenation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156250				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3145400				0	ca-XR	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145417				0	ca-XR	Manual Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154400				0	ca-XR	You can insert a hyphen where you want on a line, or let $[officename] search for the words to hyphenate, and then offer a suggested hyphenation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help					0	ca-XR	To Manually Hyphenate Single Words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	ca-XR	To quickly insert a hyphen, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Hyphen(-).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154244				0	ca-XR	If you insert a manual hyphen in a word, the word is only hyphenated at the manual hyphen. No additional automatic hyphenation is applied for this word. A word with a manual hyphen will be hyphenated without regard to the settings on the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154847				0	ca-XR	To Manually Hyphenate Text in a Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154869				0	ca-XR	Select the text that you want to hyphenate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Hyphenation\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Using Rulers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	bm_id8186284				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>rulers;using rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>horizontal rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indents; setting on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page margins on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells;adjusting the width on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting page margins and cell widths\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"ruler\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\"\>Using Rulers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067D				0	ca-XR	To show or hide rulers, choose \<emph\>View - Ruler\</emph\>. To show the vertical ruler, choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040200.xhp\" name=\"Writer - View\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - View\</emph\>\</link\>, and then select \<emph\>Vertical ruler\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Ruler\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	ca-XR	Adjusting Page Margins				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3155175				0	ca-XR	The margins of a page are indicated by the filled areas at the ends of the rulers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149038				0	ca-XR	Changing Indents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3153631				0	ca-XR	Indents are adjusted with the three small triangles on the horizontal ruler.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	26			0	ca-XR	To change the left or the right paragraph indent, select the paragraph(s) that you want change the indent for, drag the bottom left or the bottom right triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	ca-XR	To change the first line indent of a selected paragraph, drag the top left triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	ca-XR	You can also double-click anywhere on the horizontal ruler, and adjust the indents in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030000.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;protecting/unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting;tables and sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id6007263				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</item\>\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id1924802				0	ca-XR	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150114				0	ca-XR	Protecting Sections in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	ca-XR	Any section of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text document can be protected against changes with a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4545426				0	ca-XR	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the section against accidental changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	ca-XR	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	ca-XR	Select the text. Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section - Section\</emph\>, then under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> mark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> and \<emph\>With password\</emph\> check boxes. (If the section already exists: \<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>.) Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	ca-XR	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> clear the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146081				0	ca-XR	Protecting Cells in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	ca-XR	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	ca-XR	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidental changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	ca-XR	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	ca-XR	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor in the cell or select the cells. First, if necessary, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>. Then right-click the cell to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Cell - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	ca-XR	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	ca-XR	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149259				0	ca-XR	Automatic Protection of Indexes and Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	ca-XR	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	ca-XR	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidental changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767				0	ca-XR	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
