helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	49			0	ca-XR	Place the cursor in the index. First of all, if necessary, under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids \</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	ca-XR	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	ca-XR	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
