helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Object - Text Attributes\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Animation\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Effect\</item\> box, select the animation that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	ca-XR	Set the properties of the effect, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145246				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;master documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;creating/editing/exporting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subdocuments;creating/editing/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indexes; master documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"globaldoc_howtos\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc_howtos.xhp\"\>Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id1522873				0	ca-XR	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	ca-XR	To Create a Master Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	ca-XR	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Master Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	ca-XR	Open an existing document and choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	ca-XR	If you are creating a new master document, the first entry in the Navigator should be a \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text\</item\> entry. Type an introduction or enter some text. This ensures that after having edited an existing style in the master document, you see the changed style when viewing the subdocuments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Navigator\</item\> for master documents (should open automatically, else press F5 to open), click and hold the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> icon, and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	ca-XR	To insert an existing file as a subdocument, choose \<emph\>File\</emph\>, locate the file that you want to include, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145405				0	ca-XR	To create a new subdocument, choose \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, type a name for the file, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8550981				0	ca-XR	To insert some text between subdocuments, choose \<emph\>Text\</emph\>. Then type the text. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	ca-XR	To Edit a Master Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	ca-XR	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	ca-XR	To open a subdocument for editing, double-click the name of the subdocument in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155931				0	ca-XR	To remove a subdocument from the master document, right-click the subdocument in the Navigator list and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. The subdocument file is not deleted, only the entry in the Navigator is removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148677				0	ca-XR	To add text to a master document, right-click an item in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Text\</emph\>. A text section is inserted before the selected item in the master document where you can type the text that you want. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	ca-XR	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move down\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move up\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153022				0	ca-XR	To add an index, such as a table of contents, right-click in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	ca-XR	\<image id=\"img_id3148959\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20246.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148959\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	ca-XR	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	ca-XR	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	ca-XR	To Start Each Subdocument on a New Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	ca-XR	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	ca-XR	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	ca-XR	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	ca-XR	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Flow\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Breaks\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>, and then select “Page” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	ca-XR	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	ca-XR	To Export a Master Document as a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> list, select a text document file format and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8371227				0	ca-XR	The subdocuments will be exported as sections. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Sections\</item\> to unprotect and remove sections, if you prefer a plain text document without sections.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Thesaurus				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>thesaurus; related words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>related words in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spelling in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dictionaries; thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lexicon, see thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>synonyms in thesaurus\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>searching;synonyms\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"using_thesaurus\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_thesaurus.xhp\" name=\"Thesaurus\"\>Thesaurus\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820				0	ca-XR	You can use the thesaurus to look up synonyms or related terms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3155920				0	ca-XR	Click in the word that you want to look up or replace.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3155867				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Thesaurus\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F7.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149848				0	ca-XR	In the Alternatives list, click an entry to copy that related term to the "Replace with" text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	ca-XR	Optionally double-click an entry to look up related terms for that entry. On your keyboard, you can also press the arrow up or down keys to select an entry. Then press Return to replace, or press the spacebar to look up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3156263				0	ca-XR	Initially, the thesaurus uses the language of the selected word in the document, if a thesaurus library for that language is installed. The title bar of the Thesaurus dialog displays the language in use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3145113				0	ca-XR	To look up the word in a different language, click the Language button, and select one of the installed thesaurus languages. A thesaurus library may not be available for all installed languages. You can install languages with a thesaurus library from the \<link href=\"https://extensions.openoffice.org/\"\>Extensions\</link\> web page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3196263				0	ca-XR	If a thesaurus library is installed for the language of a word, the context menu of the word shows a Synonyms submenu. Select any of the terms from the submenu to replace the word.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_thesaurus.xhp	0	help	par_id3154392				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06020000.xhp\" name=\"Thesaurus\"\>Thesaurus\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147688				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>custom dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;words in user-defined dictionaries\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147688				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"delete_from_dict\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/delete_from_dict.xhp\" name=\"Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\"\>Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Writing Aids\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	ca-XR	Select the user-defined dictionary that you want to edit in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>User-defined\</item\> list, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	ca-XR	Select the word that you want to delete in the \<emph\>Word\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Merging and Splitting Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147240				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>cells; merging/splitting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; merging cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell merges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>splitting cells;by menu command\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id6618243				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"table_cellmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cellmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging and Splitting Cells\"\>Merging and Splitting Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id1211890				0	ca-XR	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell and divide it into individual cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id3463850				0	ca-XR	To Merge Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id5708792				0	ca-XR	Select the adjacent cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id6301461				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Table - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
