helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1617175				0	ca-XR	In Writer, a page number is a field that you can insert into your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id6091494				0	ca-XR	To Insert Page Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8611102				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\> to insert a page number at the current cursor position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	ca-XR	If you see the text "Page number" instead of the number, choose \<emph\>View - Field names\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	ca-XR	However, these fields will change position when you add or remove text. So it is best to insert the page number field into a header or footer that has the same position and that is repeated on every page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</item\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id2551652				0	ca-XR	To Start With a Defined Page Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	ca-XR	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	ca-XR	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Text flow\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	ca-XR	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	ca-XR	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				20200411 15:09:53
