helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	ca-XR	On the \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, select "Alphabetical Index" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3147114				0	ca-XR	If you want to use a concordance file, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Concordance file\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> area, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File\</item\> button, and then locate an existing file or create a new concordance file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_index.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	28			0	ca-XR	Set the formatting options for the index, either on the current tab, or on any of the other tabs of this dialog. For example, if you want to use single letter headings in your index, click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab, and then select \<emph\>Alphabetical delimiter\</emph\>. To change the formatting of levels in the index, click the \<emph\>Styles\</emph\> tab. 				20200411 15:09:53
