helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152887				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"autocorr_except\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autocorr_except.xhp\" name=\"Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\"\>Adding Exceptions to the AutoCorrect List\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3154254	11			0	ca-XR	You can prevent AutoCorrect from correcting specific abbreviations or words that have mixed capital letters and lowercase letters. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3155576				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Exceptions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autocorr_except.xhp	0	help	par_id3147762				0	ca-XR	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
