helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154265				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"auto_spellcheck\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_spellcheck.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Check Spelling\"\>Automatically Check Spelling\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3154664				0	ca-XR	You can have $[officename] automatically check spelling while you type and underline possible misspelt words with a red wavy line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154678				0	ca-XR	To Check Spelling Automatically While You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531	42			0	ca-XR	Activate the \<emph\>AutoSpellcheck \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155569	33			0	ca-XR	Right-click a word with a red wavy underline, and then choose a suggested replacement word from the list, or from the \<emph\>AutoCorrect \</emph\>submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759	6			0	ca-XR	If you choose a word from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoCorrect\</item\> submenu, the underlined word and the replacement word are automatically added to the AutoCorrect list for the current language. To view the AutoCorrect list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147819				0	ca-XR	You can also add the underlined word to your custom dictionary by choosing \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147220				0	ca-XR	To Exclude Words From the Spellcheck				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147263				0	ca-XR	Select the words that you want to exclude.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282				0	ca-XR	Click the Language control on the Status bar to open a menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145602				0	ca-XR	Choose “None (Do not check spelling)”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145648				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Creating a new dictionary.\"\>Creating a new dictionary.\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Changing Page Orientation (Landscape or Portrait)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation/scope\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scope of page styles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6418042				0	ca-XR	All page properties for Writer text documents, like for example the page orientation, are defined by page styles. By default, a new text document uses the “Default” page style for all pages. If you open an existing text document, different page styles may have been applied to the different pages. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id8324533				0	ca-XR	It is important to know that changes that you apply to a page property will only affect the pages that use the current page style. The current page style is listed in the Status Bar at the lower window border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	ca-XR	To Change the Page Orientation for All Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6307260				0	ca-XR	If your text document consists only of pages with the same page style, you can change the page properties directly:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7994323				0	ca-XR	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id4202398				0	ca-XR	To Change the Page Orientation Only for Some Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	ca-XR	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. Page styles define more page properties, as for example header and footer or page margins. You can either change the “Default” page style for the current document, or you can define own page styles and apply those page styles to any parts of your text. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1449324				0	ca-XR	At the end of this help page, we'll discuss the scope of page styles in detail. If you are unsure about the page style concept, please read the section at the end of this page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1480758				0	ca-XR	Unlike character styles or paragraph styles, the page styles don't know a hierarchy. You can create a new page style based on the properties of an existing page style, but when you later change the source style, the new page style does not automatically inherit the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2962126				0	ca-XR	To change the page orientation for all pages that share the same page style, you first need a page style, then apply that style:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	ca-XR	Right-click a page style and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. The new page style initially gets all properties of the selected page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	ca-XR	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "My Landscape".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page that follows a page with the new style. See the section about the scope of page styles at the end of this help page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	ca-XR	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1658375				0	ca-XR	Now you have defined a proper page style with the name "My Landscape". To apply the new style, double-click the "My Landscape" page style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. All pages in the current scope of page styles will be changed. If you defined the "next style" to be a different style, only the first page of the current scope of page styles will be changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6082949				0	ca-XR	The Scope of Page Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2858668				0	ca-XR	You should be aware of the scope of page styles in %PRODUCTNAME. Which pages of your text document get affected by editing a page style?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3278603				0	ca-XR	One Page Long Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	ca-XR	A page style can be defined to span one page only. The “First Page” style is an example. You set this property by defining another page style to be the "next style", on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	ca-XR	A one page long style starts from the lower border of the current page style range up to the next page break. The next page break appears automatically when the text flows to the next page, which is sometimes called a "soft page break". Alternatively, you can insert a manual page break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	ca-XR	To insert a manual page break at the cursor position, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> or choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\> and just click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id166020				0	ca-XR	Manually Defined Range of a Page style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	ca-XR	The “Default” page style does not set a different "next style" on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page. Instead, the "next style" is set also to be “Default”. All page styles that are followed by the same page style can span multiple pages. The lower and upper borders of the page style range are defined by "page breaks with style". All the pages between any two "page breaks with style" use the same page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	ca-XR	You can insert a "page break with style" directly at the cursor position. Alternatively, you can apply the "page break with style" property to a paragraph or to a paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6054261				0	ca-XR	Perform any one of the following commands:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1811578				0	ca-XR	To insert a "page break with style" at the cursor position, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\>, select a \<emph\>Style\</emph\> name from the listbox, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9935911				0	ca-XR	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Text Flow\</item\>. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4753868				0	ca-XR	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph style, right-click the current paragraph. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style\</item\> from the context menu. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4744407				0	ca-XR	To apply the "page break with style" property to an arbitrary paragraph style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>. Click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon. Right-click the name of the paragraph style you want to modify and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146875				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>headers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>new page styles from selection\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146875				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"change_header\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/change_header.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\"\>Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153584				0	ca-XR	You can design a page layout and then create a page style based on it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3154245				0	ca-XR	For example, you can create a page style that displays a particular header, and another page style that displays a different header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	ca-XR	Open a new text document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150532				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	ca-XR	Type a name for the page in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style name\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153184	32			0	ca-XR	Double-click the name in the list to apply the style to the current page. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155541				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the new page style from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572				0	ca-XR	Type the text that you want in the header. Position the cursor into the main text area outside of the header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155592				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147771				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page break\</item\> and then select “Default” from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	ca-XR	Repeat steps 2-6 to create a second custom page style with a different header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	ca-XR	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	ca-XR	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	ca-XR	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	ca-XR	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drag Mode\</item\> icon, and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert as Hyperlink\</item\> is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	ca-XR	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	ca-XR	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	ca-XR	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	ca-XR	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Printing Register-true				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	bm_id4825891				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>rows; register-true text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines of text; register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;register-true\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>register-true;pages and paragraphs\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spacing;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;register-true text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10652				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"registertrue\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/registertrue.xhp\"\>Printing Register-true\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065E				0	ca-XR	To Set a Document to Register-True Printing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10665				0	ca-XR	Select the whole document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10669				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	ca-XR	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Register-true\</item\> checkbox and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10678				0	ca-XR	All the paragraphs in the document will be printed register-true, unless otherwise specified.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	ca-XR	To Exempt Paragraphs From Register-True Printing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	ca-XR	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	ca-XR	Select all the paragraphs you want to exempt, then choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068C				0	ca-XR	Open the Styles and Formatting window, click the Paragraph Style you want to exempt, right-click that style, choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Indents & Spacing\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN10698				0	ca-XR	Clear the \<emph\>Register-true\</emph\> checkbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\registertrue.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AA				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030100.xhp\"\>Register-true\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Resetting Font Attributes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149963				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>formats; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>font attributes; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fonts; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resetting; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>direct formatting;exiting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exiting;direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149963				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"reset_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/reset_format.xhp\" name=\"Resetting Font Attributes\"\>Resetting Font Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154091				0	ca-XR	You can quickly exit manual formatting by pressing the right-arrow key. For example, if you have pressed Ctrl+B to apply the bold typeface to the text that you type, press the right arrow to return to the default character format of the paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	ca-XR	To reset all direct formatting of existing text, select that text, then choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Changing the Case of Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155182				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>characters; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters; text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>uppercase; formatting text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;cases of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>initial capitals in titles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>small capitals (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"text_capital\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_capital.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Case of Text\"\>Changing the Case of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	ca-XR	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	ca-XR	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	ca-XR	To Capitalize Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	ca-XR	Select the text that you want to capitalize.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	ca-XR	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485778				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485775				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select the type of capitalization in the Effects box. "Capitals" capitalizes all letters. "Title" capitalizes the first letter of each word. "Small capitals" capitalizes all letters, but in a reduced font size.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	ca-XR	To Change Text to Lowercase				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	ca-XR	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606				0	ca-XR	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id112020091049000				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910490034				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select "Lowercase" in the Effects box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	About Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>fields;updating/viewing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Help tips;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;field highlighting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;field shadings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;fields\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"fields\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"About Fields\"\>About Fields\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	ca-XR	Fields are used for data that changes in a document, such as the current date or the total number of pages in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	ca-XR	Viewing Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	ca-XR	Fields consist of a field name and the field content. To switch the field display between the field name or the field content, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"View - Fields\"\>\<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	ca-XR	To display or hide field highlighting in a document, choose \<emph\>View - Field Shadings\</emph\>. To permanently disable this feature, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Appearance\</emph\>, and clear the check box in front of \<emph\>Field shadings\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	ca-XR	To change the color of field shadings, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Appearance\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>$[officename] - Appearance\</item\>\</link\>\</emph\>, locate the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Field shadings\</item\> option, and then select a different color in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Color setting\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153166				0	ca-XR	Field Properties				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3153180				0	ca-XR	Most field types in a document, including database fields, store and display variable values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	ca-XR	The following field types execute an action when you click the field:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	ca-XR	Field Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	ca-XR	Property				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147789				0	ca-XR	Placeholder				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812				0	ca-XR	Opens a dialog to insert the object for which the placeholder was set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	ca-XR	Insert Reference				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	ca-XR	Moves the mouse pointer to the reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	ca-XR	Run macro				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147290				0	ca-XR	Runs a macro.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	ca-XR	Input Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637				0	ca-XR	Opens a dialog to edit the contents of the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3151244				0	ca-XR	Placeholder, hidden text, insert reference, variable, database, and user-defined fields display a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field in a document. To enable this feature, ensure that the Extended Tips option (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>What's This?\</item\>) is selected in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Help\</item\> menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155937				0	ca-XR	Updating Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155963				0	ca-XR	To update all of the fields in a document, press F9, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Select All\</emph\>, and then press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984				0	ca-XR	To update a field that was inserted from a database, select the field, and then press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	About Headers and Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	ca-XR	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	ca-XR	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	ca-XR	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	ca-XR	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	ca-XR	You can also choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\> tab, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer on\</item\>. Clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Same content left/right\</item\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	ca-XR	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	ca-XR	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	ca-XR	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Web Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153899				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; performing calculations in\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153899				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext2.xhp\" name=\"Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\"\>Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	ca-XR	You can perform a calculation on cells in one table and display the result in a different table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	ca-XR	Open a text document, insert a table with multiple columns and rows, and then insert another table consisting of one cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	ca-XR	Enter numbers into some of the cells of the large table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor in the table with the single cell, and then press F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155551				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	ca-XR	Click in a cell in the larger table that contains a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155598				0	ca-XR	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	ca-XR	If you want, you can format the table to behave as normal text. Insert the table into a frame, and then anchor the frame as a character. The frame remains anchored to the adjacent text when you insert or delete text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Inserting an Entire Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155185				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>sections;inserting external content\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;merging\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;inserting text documents as\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155185				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"textdoc_inframe\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/textdoc_inframe.xhp\" name=\"Inserting an Entire Text Document\"\>Inserting an Entire Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id1812799				0	ca-XR	To Insert a Text File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor in the document where you want to insert the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149839				0	ca-XR	Locate the text document that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3148858				0	ca-XR	The contents of the text document are embedded into the current document and are not updated if the source file is changed. If you want the contents to automatically update when you change the source document, insert the file as a link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	ca-XR	To Insert an Entire Text Document as a Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3150096				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor in the document where you want to insert the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	ca-XR	Type a name in the \<emph\>New Section\</emph\> box, and then select the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149642				0	ca-XR	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File Name\</item\> box, type the name of the file that you want to insert, or click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) and locate the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968				0	ca-XR	If the target text document contains sections, you can select the section that you want to insert in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sections\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	ca-XR	If you want, set the formatting options for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149862				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	ca-XR	$[officename] automatically updates the contents of the inserted section whenever the source document is changed. To manually update the contents of the section, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Update All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Printing in Reverse Order				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149688				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>ordering;printing in reverse order\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; reverse order\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149688				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"printing_order\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/printing_order.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Reverse Order\"\>Printing in Reverse Order\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3149616				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing\"\>Printing\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text\"\>Conditional Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	ca-XR	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	ca-XR	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175				0	ca-XR	To Define a Conditional Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	ca-XR	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759				0	ca-XR	Click "Set variable" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147784				0	ca-XR	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	ca-XR	Click "Text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	ca-XR	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	ca-XR	To Define a Condition and the Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659				0	ca-XR	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	ca-XR	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	ca-XR	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	ca-XR	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	ca-XR	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446				0	ca-XR	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073				0	ca-XR	To Display the Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	ca-XR	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	ca-XR	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	ca-XR	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box with 3, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	ca-XR	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145714				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of conditional operators\"\>List of conditional operators\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Emphasizing Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149820				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>text; emphasizing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>emphasizing text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasizing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	ca-XR	Here are a few examples of how to emphasize text in a document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	ca-XR	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	ca-XR	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background color, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	ca-XR	Select the text, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	ca-XR	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	ca-XR	Use Fontwork. To open the Fontwork window, click the Fontwork Gallery icon on the Drawing bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147692				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>pasting;results of formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>clipboard;calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;pasting results in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147692				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"calculate_clipboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_clipboard.xhp\" name=\" Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\"\> Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156366				0	ca-XR	If your text already contains a formula, for example "12+24*2", $[officename] can calculate, and then paste the result of the formula in your document, without using the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	ca-XR	Select the formula in the text. The formula can only contain numbers and operators and cannot contain spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155496	38			0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Calculate\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Plus Sign (+).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id5172582				0	ca-XR	Place the cursor where you want to insert the result of the formula, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste\</item\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.\<br/\>The selected formula is replaced by the result.				20200411 15:09:53
