helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147508				0	ca-XR	Index				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154103				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_INSERT_IDX_MRK_TYPE\"\>Select the index that you want to add the entry to.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153527				0	ca-XR	Entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151312				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_INSERT_IDX_MRK_ENTRY\"\>Displays the text that is selected in the document. If you want, you can enter a different word for the index entry. The selected text in the document is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154480				0	ca-XR	1st key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152953				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_INSERT_IDX_MRK_PRIM_KEY\"\>Makes the current selection a subentry of the word that you enter here. For example, if you select "cold", and enter "weather" as the 1st key, the index entry is "weather, cold".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154572				0	ca-XR	2nd key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155904				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_INSERT_IDX_MRK_SEC_KEY\"\>Makes the current selection a sub-subentry of the 1st key. For example, if you select "cold", and enter "weather" as the 1st key and "winter" as the 2nd key, the index entry is "weather, winter, cold".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155174				0	ca-XR	Phonetic reading				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_INSERT_IDX_MRK_PHONETIC_READING\"\>Enter the phonetic reading for the corresponding entry. For example, if a Japanese Kanji word has more than one pronunciation, enter the correct pronunciation as a Katakana word. The Kanji word is then sorted according to the phonetic reading entry.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if Asian language support is enabled.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143284				0	ca-XR	Main Entry				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_INSERT_IDX_MRK_MAIN_ENTRY\"\>Makes the selected text the main entry in an alphabetical index.\</ahelp\> $[officename] displays the page number of the main entry in a different format than the other entries in the index.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149821				0	ca-XR	Level				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147098				0	ca-XR	Entries using the paragraph format "Heading X" (X = 1-10) can be automatically added to the table of contents. The level of the entry in the index corresponds to the outline level of the heading style.\<ahelp hid=\"HID_INSERT_IDX_MRK_LEVEL\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149175				0	ca-XR	This option is available only for table of contents and user-defined index entries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156278				0	ca-XR	Apply to all similar texts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145783				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_INSERT_IDX_MRK_APPLY_ALL\"\>Automatically marks all other occurrences of the selected text in the document. Text in headers, footers, frames, and captions is not included.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155920	21			0	ca-XR	You cannot use the function for an \<emph\>Entry \</emph\>that you entered manually in this dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147496	18			0	ca-XR	To include all occurrences of a text passage in an index, select the text, choose\<emph\> Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>, and click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>. Then choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
