helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157557				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020100.xhp\" name=\"Section\"\>Section\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	ca-XR	Sets the properties of the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151170				0	ca-XR	New Section				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:COMBOBOX:TP_INSERT_SECTION:ED_RNAME\"\>Type a name for the new section.\</ahelp\> By default, $[officename] automatically assigns the name "Section X" to new sections, where X is a consecutive number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154102				0	ca-XR	Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149806				0	ca-XR	Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154472				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_INSERT_SECTION:CB_FILE\"\>Inserts the contents of another document or section from another document in the current section.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153672				0	ca-XR	DDE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151310	27			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:MD_EDIT_REGION:CB_DDE\"\>Creates a \<emph\>DDE \</emph\>link. Select this check box, and then enter the \<emph\>DDE \</emph\>command that you want to use. The \<emph\>DDE\</emph\> option is only available if the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box is selected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143280				0	ca-XR	The general syntax for a DDE command is: "<Server> <Topic> <Item>", where server is the DDE name for the application that contains the data. Topic refers to the location of the Item (usually the file name), and Item represents the actual object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149098	35			0	ca-XR	For example, to insert a section named "Section1" from a $[officename] text document abc.sxw as a DDE link, use the command: "soffice x:\\abc.sxw Section1". To insert the contents of the first cell from a MS Excel spreadsheet file called "abc.xls", use the command: "excel x:\\[abc.xls]Sheet1 z1s1". You can also copy the elements that you want to insert as a DDE link, and then \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>. You can then view the DDE command for the link, by selecting the contents and choosing \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153640	28			0	ca-XR	File name\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\> / DDE command \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04020100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145754	29			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:MD_EDIT_REGION:ED_FILE\"\>Enter the path and the filename for the file that you want to insert, or click the browse button (\<emph\>...\</emph\>) to locate the file.\</ahelp\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the \<emph\>DDE \</emph\>check box is selected, enter the DDE command that you want to use. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
