helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Navigation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147745				0	ca-XR	Navigation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149844				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCRL_NAVI\"\>If you click this icon, a toolbar will appear which enables you to choose among the existing targets within a document.\</ahelp\> You can then use the up and down arrow icons to position the text cursor in the document on the previous or next target.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153293				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCRL_PAGEUP\"\>Click the up button to scroll to the previous page or object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156098				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCRL_PAGEDOWN\"\>Click the down button to scroll to the next page or object.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155076				0	ca-XR	By default, as long as you have not selected any other entry, the arrow buttons jump to the previous or the next page in the document. The arrow buttons are black if you are browsing through pages and blue if you jump to other objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154330				0	ca-XR	The entries largely correspond to those in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> selection box. You can also select other jump destinations. An example are the reminders, which you can set with the \<emph\>Set Reminder\</emph\> icon in the Navigator. You can select an object from among the following options on the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar: table, text frame, graphics, OLE object, page, headings, reminder, drawing object, control field, section, bookmark, selection, footnote, note, index entry, table formula, wrong table formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148783				0	ca-XR	For table formulas, you can either jump to all table formulas located within your document or only to the incorrect ones. For incorrect formulas, you jump only to formulas that have resulted in errors. The program skips over formulas with resulting errors (those that reference incorrect formulas).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150031				0	ca-XR	Working With the Navigation Toolbar				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	ca-XR	Open the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar by clicking on its icon located in the vertical scrollbar. You can break the toolbar away from its place by dragging and arrange it on the screen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153141				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_NAVI_VS\"\>Click the icon for the type of objects you want to browse through. Then click one of the "Previous Object" or "Next Object" arrow buttons. The names of these buttons indicate the type of object you have selected. The text cursor is placed on whichever object you have selected.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968				0	ca-XR	You can configure $[officename] according to your specific preferences for navigating within a document. To do this, choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>\</link\>. The various tables for adapting \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140100.xhp\" name=\"menus\"\>menus\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140200.xhp\" name=\"keyboard input\"\>keyboard input\</link\> or toolbars contain various functions for navigation within the document under the "Navigate" area. In this way you can jump to the index tags in the document with the "To Next/Previous Index Tag" functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155338				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>searching; repeating a search\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155338				0	ca-XR	Repeat Search				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\02110100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155361				0	ca-XR	With the \<emph\>Repeat search\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar you can repeat a search you started with the \<emph\>Search and Replace\</emph\> dialog. To do this, click the icon. The blue arrow buttons on the vertical scrollbar now take on the functions \<emph\>Continue search forwards\</emph\> and \<emph\>Continue search backwards\</emph\>. If you now click one of the arrow surfaces, the search will be continued for the term entered in the Search and Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
