helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150147				0	ca-XR	For example, to hide a paragraph, text, or a section from a user with a specific initial, such as "LM", enter the condition: user_initials=="LM".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154115				0	ca-XR	Conditions and Database Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154128				0	ca-XR	You can define conditions for accessing databases, or database fields. For example, you can check the contents of a database field from a condition, or use database fields in logical expressions. The following table lists a few more examples of using databases in conditions:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156066				0	ca-XR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156088				0	ca-XR	Meaning				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155948				0	ca-XR	Database.Table.Company				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	ca-XR	Database.Table.Company NEQ ""				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148687				0	ca-XR	Database.Table.Company != ""				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373				0	ca-XR	The condition is true if the COMPANY field is not empty. (In the first example, no operator is required.)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149977				0	ca-XR	!Database.Table.Company				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	ca-XR	NOT Database.Table.Company				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150004				0	ca-XR	Database.Table.Company EQ ""				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146911				0	ca-XR	Database.Table.Company ==""				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733				0	ca-XR	Returns TRUE if the COMPANY field is empty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148762				0	ca-XR	Database.Table.Company !="Sun"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153016				0	ca-XR	Database.Table.Company NEQ "Sun"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153040				0	ca-XR	Returns TRUE if the current entry in the COMPANY field is not "Sun". (Exclamation sign represents a logical NOT.)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154605				0	ca-XR	Database.Table.Firstname AND Database.Table.Name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153059				0	ca-XR	Returns TRUE if the record contains the first and the last name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159247				0	ca-XR	Note the difference between the boolean NOT "!" and the comparative operator not equal "!=" (NEQ).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	ca-XR	When you refer to a database field in a condition, use the form Databasename.Tablename.Fieldname. If one of the names contains a character that is an operator, such as a minus sign (-), enclose the name in square brackets, for example, Databasename.[Table-name].Fieldname. Never use spaces inside field names.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153891				0	ca-XR	Example: Hiding an Empty Database Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	ca-XR	You may want to create a condition that hides an empty field, for example, if the COMPANY field is empty for some of the data records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150067				0	ca-XR	Select the \<emph\>Hidden Paragraph\</emph\> list entry, and type the following condition: Addressbook.Addresses.Company EQ ""				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	ca-XR	or type the following				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	ca-XR	NOT Addressbook.Addresses.Company				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147136				0	ca-XR	If the COMPANY database field is empty, the condition is true and the paragraph is hidden.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150232				0	ca-XR	To display hidden paragraphs on the screen, you can choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>, and clear the \<emph\>Fields: Hidden paragraphs\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145218				0	ca-XR	Examples of Conditions in Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145231				0	ca-XR	The following examples use the Conditional text field, although they can be applied to any fields that can be linked to a condition. The syntax used for conditions is also used for the Hidden text, Hidden paragraph, Any record or Next record fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150311				0	ca-XR	To display conditional text based on the number of pages:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147471				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, click "Conditional text".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154294	63			0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box, type "page == 1".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box, type "There is only one page".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640	65			0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box, type "There are several pages".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153086				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155814				0	ca-XR	To display conditional text based on a user-defined Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155836				0	ca-XR	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Variables\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155109	68			0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list, click "Set Variable".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	139			0	ca-XR	In the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, type "Profit".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147032	140			0	ca-XR	In the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box, type "5000".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152974				0	ca-XR	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152998				0	ca-XR	Click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab, and click "Conditional text" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, type "Profit < 5000".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box, type "Target is not met".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156317	72			0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box, type "Target is met".				20200411 15:09:53
