helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"seitetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PageDialog\"\>Specify the formatting styles and the layout for the current page style, including page margins, headers and footers, and the page background.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154505				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Field Names\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Fieldnames\"\>Switches the field display between field names and field contents.\</ahelp\> A check mark indicates that the field names are displayed, and no check mark indicates that field contents are displayed. Some field contents cannot be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287	4			0	ca-XR	To change the default field display to field names instead of the field contents, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - View\</emph\>, and then select the\<emph\> Field codes \</emph\>checkbox in the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	ca-XR	When you print a document with \<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\> enabled, you are prompted to include the field names in the print out.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145579				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Fields\"\>Insert - Fields\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
