helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	bm_id				0	ca-XR	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;headings\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>headings;automatic\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>separator lines;AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155962				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150200.xhp\" name=\"Apply\"\>Apply\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871	2			0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoFormatApply\"\>Automatically formats the file according to the options that you set under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>            \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404				0	ca-XR	When you apply automatic formats, the following rules apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155625				0	ca-XR	AutoCorrect for Headings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505				0	ca-XR	A paragraph is formatted as a heading when the following conditions are met:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	ca-XR	paragraph begins with a capital letter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148386				0	ca-XR	paragraph does not end with a punctuation mark				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150564				0	ca-XR	empty paragraph above and below the paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149030				0	ca-XR	AutoCorrect for Bullets / Numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	ca-XR	To create a bulleted list, type a hyphen (-), star (*), or plus sign (+), followed by a space or tab at the beginning of a paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150763	18			0	ca-XR	To create a numbered list, type a number followed by a period (.), followed by a space or tab at the beginning of a paragraph. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147507				0	ca-XR	Automatic numbering is only applied to paragraphs formatted with the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\>, \<emph\>Text body\</emph\> or \<emph\>Text body indent\</emph\> paragraph styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152941				0	ca-XR	AutoCorrect for Separator Lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154105				0	ca-XR	If you type three or more hyphens (---), underscores (___) or equal signs (===) on line and then press Enter, the paragraph is replaced by a horizontal line as wide as the page. The line is actually the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"lower border\"\>lower border\</link\> of the preceding paragraph. The following rules apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153530				0	ca-XR	Three hyphens (-) yield a single line (0.05 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477				0	ca-XR	Three underscore (_) yield a single line (1 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	ca-XR	Three equal signs (=) yield a double line (1.10 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
