helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	ca-XR	Use this area to specify which information to include in an index.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149815				0	ca-XR	Outline				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3151253				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_FROMHEADINGS\"\>Creates the index using outline levels, that is, paragraphs formatted with one of the predefined heading styles (Heading 1-10) are added to the index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id1209200804373840				0	ca-XR	You can also assign the outline levels in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\"\>Outline & Numbering\</link\> tab page of the Format - Paragraph dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153633				0	ca-XR	Additional Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"vorlg\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_ADDSTYLES\"\>Includes the paragraph styles that you specify in the \<emph\>Assign Styles\</emph\> dialog as index entries. To select the paragraph styles that you want to include in the index, click the \<emph\>Assign Styles (...\</emph\>) button to the right of this box.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149168				0	ca-XR	...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3145776				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_SELECT:PB_ADDSTYLES\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Assign Styles\</emph\> dialog, where you can select the paragraph styles to include in the index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151374				0	ca-XR	Index marks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_TOXMARKS\"\>Includes the index entries that you inserted by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\> in the index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149871				0	ca-XR	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3148569				0	ca-XR	Specifies the number of columns and the column layout for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	ca-XR	Sections follow the text flow behavior of the page they are inserted into.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3083448				0	ca-XR	For example, if you insert a section that uses a two-column layout into a page style that uses a four-column layout, the two-column layout is nested inside one of the four columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040501.xhp	0	help	par_id3155625				0	ca-XR	You can also nest sections, that is, you can insert a section into another section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Unprotect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149052				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05100400.xhp\" name=\"Unprotect\"\>Unprotect\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3083450				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UnsetCellsReadOnly\"\>Removes the cell protection for all selected cells in the current table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	3			0	ca-XR	To remove the protection from several tables at once, select the tables, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+T. To remove the protection from all of the tables in a document, click anywhere in the document, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+T.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150765				0	ca-XR	You can also remove cell protection from a table in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Index				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147338				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120212.xhp\" name=\"Index\"\>Index\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962	2			0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"verzeichnis\"\>The following options are available when you select \<emph\>Alphabetical Index \</emph\>as the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index\"\>index\</link\> type. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153247				0	ca-XR	Options				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154651				0	ca-XR	Combine identical entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_COLLECTSAME\"\>Replaces identical index entries with a single entry that lists the page numbers where the entry occurs in the document. For example, the entries "View 10, View 43" are combined as "View 10, 43".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147403				0	ca-XR	Combine identical entries with p or pp				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3083451				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_USEFF\"\>Replaces identical index entries, which occur also on the directly following page or pages, with a single entry that lists the first page number and a "p" or "pp". For example, the entries "View 10, View 11, View 12" are combined as "View 10pp", and "View 10, View 11" as "View 10p".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157870				0	ca-XR	Combine with -				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3145825				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_USE_DASH\"\>Replaces identical index entries that occur on consecutive pages with a single entry and the page range where the entry occurs. For example, the entries "View 10, View 11, View 12" are combined as "View 10-12".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154502				0	ca-XR	Case sensitive				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3149880				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_CASESENSITIVE\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters in identical index entries. For Asian languages special handling applies.\</ahelp\> If you want the first occurrence of the entry in the document to determine the case of the entry, select \<emph\>Combine identical entries\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	ca-XR	To use multi-level collation to Asian languages, select \<emph\>Case sensitive\</emph\>. In the multi-level collation, the cases and diacritics of the entries are ignored and only the primitive forms of the entries are compared. If the forms are identical, the diacritics of the forms are compared. If the forms are still identical, the cases of the forms as well as the widths of the characters, and the differences in the Japanese Kana are compared.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150569				0	ca-XR	AutoCapitalize entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3148772				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_INITIALCAPS\"\>Automatically capitalizes the first letter of an index entry.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155986				0	ca-XR	Keys as separate entries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3147170				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_KEYASENTRY\"\>Inserts index keys as separate index entries.\</ahelp\> A key is inserted as a top level index entry and the entries that are assigned to the key as indented subentries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3151184				0	ca-XR	To define an index key, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120100.xhp\" name=\"Insert Index Entry\"\>\<emph\>Insert Index Entry\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154646				0	ca-XR	Concordance file				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120212.xhp	0	help	par_id3156322				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_TOX_SELECT_CB_FROMFILE\"\>Automatically marks index entries using a concordance file - a list of words to include in an index.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
