helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05200000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154652				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05200000.xhp\" name=\"Merge Table\"\>Merge Table\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05200000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147401				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:MergeTable\"\>Combines two consecutive tables into a single table. The tables must be directly next to each other and not separated by an empty paragraph.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05200000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146325				0	ca-XR	If you choose this command when the cursor is in the middle of three consecutive tables, you are prompted to select the table that you want to merge with.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	ca-XR	Nonprinting Characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154507				0	ca-XR	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"Nonprinting Characters\"\>Nonprinting Characters\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154646				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ControlCodes\"\>Shows nonprinting characters in your text, such as paragraph marks, line breaks, tab stops, and spaces.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145410				0	ca-XR	When you delete a paragraph mark, the paragraph that is merged takes on the formatting of the paragraph that the cursor is in.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147511				0	ca-XR	To specify which nonprinting characters are displayed, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Writer - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want in the \<emph\>Display of\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
