helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149805				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_LINE\"\>Ends the current line, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the next line, without creating a new paragraph.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149685				0	ca-XR	You can also insert a line break by pressing Shift+Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148566				0	ca-XR	Column Break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_COL\"\>Inserts a manual column break (in a multiple column layout), and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040500.xhp\" name=\"column\"\>column\</link\>. A manual column break is indicated by a nonprinting border at the top of the new column.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	ca-XR	Page Break				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149102				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_BREAK:RB_PAGE\"\>Inserts a manual page break, and moves the text found to the right of the cursor to the beginning of the next page. The inserted page break is indicated by a nonprinting border at the top of the new page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145758	13			0	ca-XR	You can also insert a page break by pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter. However, if you want to assign the following page a different Page Style, you must use the menu command to insert the manual page break.				20200411 15:09:53
