helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159212				0	ca-XR	Inserts the current page number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159229				0	ca-XR	In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, click the numbering format that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145188	39			0	ca-XR	If you want, you can enter an \<emph\>Offset \</emph\>for the displayed page number. With an \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value of 1, the field will display a number that is 1 more than the current page number, but only if a page with that number exists. On the last page of the document, this same field will be empty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150891				0	ca-XR	Offset				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155312				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:TP_FLD_DOK:ED_DOKVALUE\"\>Enter the offset value that you want to apply to a page number field, for example "+1".\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948				0	ca-XR	If you want to change the actual page number and not the displayed number, do not use the \<emph\>Offset\</emph\> value. To change page numbers, read the \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>\<emph\>Page Numbers\</emph\>\</link\> guide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145595				0	ca-XR	Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145613				0	ca-XR	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKFORMAT\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150138				0	ca-XR	\<variable id=\"datumuhrzeitformat\"\>When you click "Additional formats", the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialog opens, where you can define a custom format. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154867				0	ca-XR	If you choose "Chapter number without separator" for a chapter field, the separators that are specified for chapter number in \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Outline numbering\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Outline numbering\</emph\>\</link\> are not displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156079				0	ca-XR	If you choose "chapter number" as the \<emph\>format\</emph\> for reference fields, only the number of the chapter heading containing the referenced object is displayed in the field. If the paragraph style for the chapter heading is not numbered, the field is left blank.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148682				0	ca-XR	The following number range formats are for paragraphs formatted with numbered or bulleted lists:				20200411 15:09:53
